-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Driver.CLI.adam - adam's command line

  RunCommandLine reads argv through the paramcount / paramstr intrinsics and
  drives one Adam.Driver.Compiler. Everything the command line knows is in
  two tables, and both the reader and the help read only them:

    DoCommandTable   every command: its word, its one positional argument
                     (a file; a file or a project folder; a help topic) as
                     the help writes it, its summary, its examples
    DoOptionTable    every option: its short and long forms, the value it
                     takes ("" = a flag), its summary, the commands it
                     belongs to (none listed = every command); DoApply is
                     its handler, by its CLIOption

  build's argument is a main module's file, or a project folder whose
  project.toml names the main module (none given: the current folder),
  never one searched for above it, as PaskalCPP's build [<folder>]: no
  project.toml there is CL0013 (exit 2), one that does not load its PJ
  reports (exit 1). check takes a file only. init takes two arguments, the
  new project's name and its type (PaskalCPP's init <name> <exe|dll|lib>):
  one missing is CL0015, a type that is not exe, dll or lib CL0016 (both
  exit 2); Adam.Driver.Project's Scaffold makes the project in the working
  folder (its PJ reports, exit 1) and two status lines say where and how to
  build it (not under --quiet). pack takes a project folder as build does
  (PaskalCPP's pack [<folder>], built into adam: no packer program): the
  project's assets folder zipped by System.CustomIO's ZipDirectoryContents
  into <name>.rez in its output folder (one archive for every target and
  mode), with its pack password; every project build copies it beside the
  exe it writes, and pack updates each copy an earlier build left; no
  assets folder is CL0017, the archive's folder, the archive itself or a
  copy CL0018 / CL0019 / CL0021 (exit 1); each entry, the count, the
  archive and each updated copy are printed (not under --quiet). cimport
  takes an import spec (<name>.cimport.toml, Adam.CImport.Spec): its C
  headers found by Adam.CImport.Headers over the spec's include folders and
  the target's system headers (-t, else the registry's default), its
  <unit>.adam placed in -o, else the spec's output folder, else beside the
  spec; the headers preprocessed (Adam.CImport.Preprocessor: the target's
  predefines, the spec's defines and undefines, then each header as an
  #include <name>); no spec given is CL0024 (exit 2), the spec's, the
  search's and the preprocessor's CP errors exit 1; not under --quiet the
  import's line and each header's are printed; --emit-pp prints the
  preprocessed tokens (clang -E's text) after them, quiet or not, and stops
  there, as clang -E does. Else the tokens are parsed (Adam.CImport.Parser:
  CC errors exit 1) and the unit written (Adam.CImport.Writer, the
  declarations of the spec's sources folders, by default each header's own
  folder; CI reports; a file that cannot be written CI0004) to its file;
  --emit-unit prints its text, not under --quiet the count line follows.
  Then (M9g) when the spec's layoutprobe is true or --emit-layout is given,
  the unit written is checked by Adam's front end (Compiler.CheckUnit, its
  errors exit 1) and its layout probe made (Adam.CImport.LayoutProbe): the
  spec's layoutprobe writes it to <unit>.layout.c beside the unit (not under
  --quiet its line printed), --emit-layout prints it after the unit's text.

  A new command or option is one more table entry (and its handler): the
  reader, the help's rows and columns and the mistakes follow from it. The
  targets are Adam.Target.Registry's: -t (a name or a triple) is checked
  against it, and the help of adam and of every command that takes -t lists
  what it holds (the default marked), so a target added there reaches the
  command line by itself; no target is named in any text here.

  The line: options anywhere, a value-taking option takes the next argument
  whatever it is; the first other argument is the command, the next its
  positional argument. No command: adam's help. -h / --help: the help of the
  command given, else adam's. The banner (adam's name and version, its
  copyright and its link, all Adam.Core.Common's identity) comes first unless
  --no-banner is given. In the help, a command's argument and an option's
  value are placeholders: each list's names in a column of their own, the
  placeholders lined up after it. A '--' ends adam's own arguments: every one
  after it is the program's, for build -r, which runs the exe it wrote in
  the folder it landed in, on adam's own console (System.IO's
  RunAttached), adam's exit code then the program's; or for build -d
  (M11a D4), which runs it under Adam's console debugger (Adam.Debug.REPL
  over the debug parts Adam.Debug.Targets picks for its triple), adam's
  exit code then the program's last run's: it needs a debug build (its
  debug file, Compiler.DebugFilePath; none is CL0025), and -r with -d is
  CL0026.

  What needs the host's debugger part (build -d, --host, adam dap, adam
  editor: CommandSpec / OptionSpec.Debugger) is in the help and the reader
  only on a host this adam has one for (Adam.Debug.Targets: win64 today);
  elsewhere it is not listed and, given anyway, CL0033 (not unknown).

  adam dap (M11a D5) serves the Debug Adapter Protocol on stdin / stdout for
  an editor (Adam.Debug.DAP over Adam.Protocol.Stdio's channel): nothing else
  is written to stdout, the banner neither; a source the client launches is
  built for debugging here (CLIDAPBuilder: a debug build, its reports as the
  client's output). It takes no argument (CL0027). A noDebug launch (an
  editor's Run) is built at the launch's "optimize" level where the main
  module's @optimize names none, else at its own.

  adam lsp (M11b) serves the Language Server Protocol on stdin / stdout for an
  editor (Adam.LSP.Server over Adam.Protocol.Stdio's channel), as adam dap
  does: nothing else on stdout, no banner, no argument (CL0027); its checks
  are this compiler's front end with its own module paths.

  adam info [<folder>] (M11a D5e) prints the project whose project.toml is
  in the folder (none given: the current folder, never searched for above
  it) as one line of JSON for an editor, so editor and compiler never
  disagree on a project (pcpp's --project-info): format (ADAM_CLI_INFO_FORMAT),
  project (the file is there), valid (it loaded), root, and when valid file,
  name, kind (exe / dll / lib), main, output, rez (paths in '/' form); reports
  [{severity, code, message}] every report the load made. No banner (stdout
  is the JSON); exit ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK whenever the line is written, the
  project valid or not. --defaults (build, check) makes -t / -opt the
  main module's defaults (Compiler.SetDefaultTarget / SetDefaultLevel): they
  stand in only where it names no @target / @optimize, as an editor's
  toolbar does; without it they win over the source.

  On a console that takes VT sequences (System.Console's EscapesEnabled)
  the banner, the help (HelpOut) and every report's severity word
  (Diagnostics.SetColor) are in color; piped or redirected, every line is
  plain text, byte for byte what the rows compare.

  A build never looks hung (CLIPhases): on such a console the running
  phase's line is drawn in place and redrawn as each step starts (the unit
  and its step: `Lowering 12/68 Adam.Opt.Gvn: optimize ... 23s`) and each
  second by a ticker task, then overwritten by the phase's final line;
  piped, redirected or under --quiet only the final lines print.

  A command line mistake is one Error with no place (CL codes, texts in
  Adam.Core.Messages) ending in the help to see, reported into the compile's
  own Diagnostics, so every line adam prints has one form. Exit codes:
  ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK / ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS from the compile (the help
  is ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK), ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE for a mistake. CL0001 (the
  old one-line usage) is retired: its number is not reused.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Driver.CLI;

import System.SysUtils, System.IO, System.Process, System.Runtime, System.CustomIO, System.Console,
  Adam.Core.Common,
  Adam.Core.Messages, Adam.Target, Adam.Target.Registry, Adam.Compiler.SourceText,
  Adam.Compiler.Diagnostics, Adam.ACU.Format, Adam.CImport.Spec, Adam.CImport.Headers,
  Adam.CImport.Preprocessor, Adam.CImport.Parser, Adam.CImport.Writer, Adam.CImport.Merge,
  Adam.CImport.LayoutProbe,
  Adam.Driver.Project, Adam.Driver.Compiler, Adam.Debug.Targets, Adam.Debug.REPL,
  Adam.Protocol.Transport, Adam.Protocol.Stdio, Adam.Debug.DAP, Adam.LSP.Server, System.JSON.Ext,
  Adam.Dev.Editor, Adam.Dev.BuildAdam, Adam.Dev.Pack;

public const
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_002: string = "CL0002";   // not a command
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_003: string = "CL0003";   // a command with no file
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_004: string = "CL0004";   // one positional argument too many
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_005: string = "CL0005";   // not an option (of the command given)
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_006: string = "CL0006";   // help of what is not a command
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_007: string = "CL0007";   // an option with no value after it
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_008: string = "CL0008";   // an option given twice
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_009: string = "CL0009";   // -t names no target the registry has
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_010: string = "CL0010";   // '--' (the program's arguments) without -r
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_011: string = "CL0011";   // -r: the exe could not be started
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_012: string = "CL0012";   // -r: the exe's target does not run on this machine
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_013: string = "CL0013";   // build <folder>: no project.toml in that folder
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_014: string = "CL0014";   // build <folder>: the folder cannot be resolved
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_015: string = "CL0015";   // init: the name or the type is missing
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_016: string = "CL0016";   // init: the type is not exe, dll or lib
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_017: string = "CL0017";   // pack: the project has no assets folder
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_018: string = "CL0018";   // pack: the archive's folder cannot be made
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_019: string = "CL0019";   // pack: the archive cannot be written
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_020: string = "CL0020";   // -opt names no optimization level
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_021: string = "CL0021";   // pack: a copy beside a built exe cannot be updated
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_022: string = "CL0022";   // (warning) -r on a dll, which no process runs
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_023: string = "CL0023";   // (warning) -r on a lib, which a program links in
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_024: string = "CL0024";   // cimport with no import spec
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_025: string = "CL0025";   // -d on a build with no debug information
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_026: string = "CL0026";   // -r and -d together
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_027: string = "CL0027";   // an argument to a command that takes none
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_028: string = "CL0028";   // --host without -d
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_029: string = "CL0029";   // -d on a dll with no --host
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_030: string = "CL0030";   // --host on a build that wrote a program, not a dll
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_031: string = "CL0031";   // editor: the editor is not beside adam
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_032: string = "CL0032";   // editor: the editor could not be started
  ADAM_ERR_CLI_033: string = "CL0033";   // a command / option this host lacks (its debugger's)

  // The commands, as the user types them
  ADAM_CLI_BUILD: string = "build";
  ADAM_CLI_CHECK: string = "check";
  ADAM_CLI_INIT: string = "init";
  ADAM_CLI_PACK: string = "pack";
  ADAM_CLI_CIMPORT: string = "cimport";
  ADAM_CLI_DAP: string = "dap";
  ADAM_CLI_LSP: string = "lsp";
  ADAM_CLI_INFO: string = "info";
  ADAM_CLI_EDITOR: string = "editor";
  // The editor adam editor starts: the packaged one in res\editor\<host> beside adam (D5e)
  ADAM_CLI_EDITOR_EXE: string = ADAM_EDITOR_FOLDER + "/editor" + ADAM_HOST_EXE_EXT;
  ADAM_CLI_HELP: string = "help";

  // The options, as the user types them
  ADAM_CLI_OUTPUT_SHORT: string = "-o";
  ADAM_CLI_OUTPUT_LONG: string = "--output";
  ADAM_CLI_TARGET_SHORT: string = "-t";
  ADAM_CLI_TARGET_LONG: string = "--target";
  ADAM_CLI_OPTIMIZE_SHORT: string = "-opt";
  ADAM_CLI_OPTIMIZE_LONG: string = "--optimize";
  ADAM_CLI_DEFAULTS_LONG: string = "--defaults";
  ADAM_CLI_NO_BANNER_LONG: string = "--no-banner";
  ADAM_CLI_QUIET_SHORT: string = "-q";
  ADAM_CLI_QUIET_LONG: string = "--quiet";
  ADAM_CLI_HEAP_LONG: string = "--heap";
  ADAM_CLI_EMIT_IR_LONG: string = "--emit-ir";
  ADAM_CLI_EMIT_PP_LONG: string = "--emit-pp";
  ADAM_CLI_EMIT_UNIT_LONG: string = "--emit-unit";
  ADAM_CLI_EMIT_LAYOUT_LONG: string = "--emit-layout";
  // The compiler's own build (build-adam passes it on every stage): never public, in no
  // option table and no help; the build is a release one at safe unless -opt names another
  // level (no leak tracker, site stores or site table), its other self-build paths to come
  ADAM_CLI_SELF_BUILD_LONG: string = "--adam-self-build";
  // A developer's job, never public either (in no option table and no help, as pcpp's
  // pcppdev): the editor's app.asar packed from its source and its editor.exe stamped
  // (Adam.Dev.Editor), run in place of any command
  ADAM_CLI_DEV_EDITOR_LONG: string = "--dev-editor";
  // The same kind of job: Adam builds itself on this host (Adam.Dev.BuildAdam), run in place
  // of any command; build-adam.cmd / build-adam.sh pass it
  ADAM_CLI_DEV_BUILD_ADAM_LONG: string = "--dev-build-adam";
  // The same kind of job: the zips a TOML pack spec describes (Adam.Dev.Pack over std
  // System.Pack), the spec the argument after it; _distro.cmd / _checkpoint.cmd pass it
  ADAM_CLI_DEV_PACK_LONG: string = "--dev-pack";
  ADAM_CLI_HELP_SHORT: string = "-h";
  ADAM_CLI_HELP_LONG: string = "--help";
  ADAM_CLI_RUN_SHORT: string = "-r";
  ADAM_CLI_RUN_LONG: string = "--run";
  ADAM_CLI_DEBUG_SHORT: string = "-d";
  ADAM_CLI_DEBUG_LONG: string = "--debug";
  ADAM_CLI_HOST_LONG: string = "--host";

  // What ends adam's own arguments: every one after it is the program's (-r)
  ADAM_CLI_ARGS_SEPARATOR: string = "--";

  // The program's own name, what an option outside any command belongs to
  ADAM_CLI_PROGRAM: string = "adam";

  // The help's indent and the gap between its two columns
  ADAM_CLI_INDENT: string = "  ";
  ADAM_CLI_GAP: string = "  ";

  // The exit code of a command line mistake (no compile ran)
  ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE: int32 = 2;

  // adam info's JSON: its format (an editor reading another one sees no project) and how
  // many reports a load keeps
  ADAM_CLI_INFO_FORMAT: int64 = 1;
  ADAM_CLI_INFO_REPORT_BUDGET: int64 = 1000;

type
  // adam's commands
  CLICommand = choices(Build, Check, Init, Pack, Info, CImport, DAP, LSP, Editor, Help);

  // What a command's positional arguments are: a main module's file (required), a main
  // module's file or a project folder (none: the current folder), a help topic, a new
  // project's name and type (two, both required), a project folder (none: the current
  // folder), an import spec (required), none (an argument is CL0027)
  CLIPositional = choices(File, Project, Topic, NewProject, Folder, Spec, Files, None);

  // adam's options, each one's handler picked by it (DoApply)
  CLIOption = choices(Output, Target, Optimize, Defaults, Run, Debug, Host, EmitIR, EmitPp,
    EmitUnit, EmitLayout, NoBanner, Quiet, Heap, Help);

  // The commands an option belongs to
  CLICommandArray = array of CLICommand;

  // One command, as the reader and the help see it
  CommandSpec = record
    Id: CLICommand;
    Word: string;
    Positional: CLIPositional;
    Argument: string;
    Summary: string;
    Examples: StringArray;
    // Needs this adam's debugger part for its host's programs (dap, editor): a host with none
    // leaves it out of the help and reports it as CL0033
    Debugger: bool;
  end;

  // Every command, in the order the help lists them
  CommandTable = array of CommandSpec;

  // One option, as the reader and the help see it
  OptionSpec = record
    Id: CLIOption;
    Short: string;
    Long: string;
    Value: string;
    Summary: string;
    Commands: CLICommandArray;
    // Needs the host's debugger part (-d, --host), as CommandSpec.Debugger
    Debugger: bool;
  end;

  // Every option, in the order the help lists them
  OptionTable = array of OptionSpec;

  // One command line, as read: Command an index into the command table (-1 = none given);
  // TargetText what -t gave as typed, TargetTriple the triple of the registry's target it
  // names; LevelText what -opt gave as typed, Level the level it names when LevelGiven; Run
  // -r given, RunArgs the arguments after '--' (the program's own); TypeText init's second
  // argument (the project type as typed), "" for every other command
  CLIRequest = record
    Command: int64;
    Positional: string;
    TypeText: string;
    // editor's files, every one as typed (CLIPositional.Files: any number)
    Files: StringArray;
    Output: string;
    TargetText: string;
    TargetTriple: string;
    LevelText: string;
    Level: OptLevel;
    LevelGiven: bool;
    // --defaults given: -t / -opt only stand in where the main module names none
    Defaults: bool;
    Run: bool;
    // -d given: the exe built runs under the console debugger (RunArgs its arguments too)
    Debug: bool;
    // --host <exe>: -d on a dll debugs it in this exe, which loads it ("" none)
    HostPath: string;
    RunArgs: StringArray;
    // --emit-ir was given: the build writes <stem>.ir beside its exe
    EmitIR: bool;
    // --emit-pp was given: cimport prints its preprocessed headers (clang -E's text)
    EmitPp: bool;
    // --emit-unit was given: cimport prints the unit it wrote
    EmitUnit: bool;
    // --emit-layout was given: cimport prints the unit's layout probe (M9g)
    EmitLayout: bool;
    NoBanner: bool;
    Quiet: bool;
    Heap: bool;
    WantHelp: bool;
    // --adam-self-build was given (ADAM_CLI_SELF_BUILD_LONG)
    SelfBuild: bool;
    // --dev-editor was given (ADAM_CLI_DEV_EDITOR_LONG)
    DevEditor: bool;
    // --dev-build-adam was given (ADAM_CLI_DEV_BUILD_ADAM_LONG)
    DevBuildAdam: bool;
    // --dev-pack was given (ADAM_CLI_DEV_PACK_LONG), and the spec after it ("" when none)
    DevPack: bool;
    DevPackSpec: string;
  end;

// Adds AText at the end of AList
func DoAddString(var AList: StringArray; const AText: string);
var
  LCount: int64;
begin
  LCount := len(AList);
  setlength(AList, LCount + 1);
  AList[LCount] := AText;
end;

// Adds ACommand at the end of AList
func DoAddCommandId(var AList: CLICommandArray; const ACommand: CLICommand);
var
  LCount: int64;
begin
  LCount := len(AList);
  setlength(AList, LCount + 1);
  AList[LCount] := ACommand;
end;

// A command with no examples yet
func DoCommand(const AId: CLICommand; const AWord: string; const APositional: CLIPositional;
  const AArgument: string; const ASummary: string): CommandSpec;
var
  LSpec: CommandSpec;
begin
  LSpec.Id := AId;
  LSpec.Word := AWord;
  LSpec.Positional := APositional;
  LSpec.Argument := AArgument;
  LSpec.Summary := ASummary;
  setlength(LSpec.Examples, 0);
  LSpec.Debugger := false;
  return LSpec;
end;

// Adds ASpec at the end of ATable
func DoAddCommand(var ATable: CommandTable; const ASpec: CommandSpec);
var
  LCount: int64;
begin
  LCount := len(ATable);
  setlength(ATable, LCount + 1);
  ATable[LCount] := ASpec;
end;

// Every command (see the header)
func DoCommandTable(): CommandTable;
var
  LTable: CommandTable;
  LSpec: CommandSpec;
begin
  setlength(LTable, 0);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Build, ADAM_CLI_BUILD, CLIPositional.Project,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_PROJECT, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_BUILD);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_BUILD);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_BUILD_OUTPUT);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_BUILD_PROJECT);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Check, ADAM_CLI_CHECK, CLIPositional.File, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_FILE,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_CHECK);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_CHECK);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Init, ADAM_CLI_INIT, CLIPositional.NewProject,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_NEW_PROJECT, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_INIT);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_INIT);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Pack, ADAM_CLI_PACK, CLIPositional.Folder, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_FOLDER,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_PACK);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_PACK);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Info, ADAM_CLI_INFO, CLIPositional.Folder, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_FOLDER,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_INFO);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_INFO);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.CImport, ADAM_CLI_CIMPORT, CLIPositional.Spec,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_SPEC, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_CIMPORT);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_CIMPORT);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.DAP, ADAM_CLI_DAP, CLIPositional.None, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_DAP);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_DAP);
  LSpec.Debugger := true;
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.LSP, ADAM_CLI_LSP, CLIPositional.None, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_LSP);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_LSP);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Editor, ADAM_CLI_EDITOR, CLIPositional.Files, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_FILES,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_EDITOR);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_EDITOR);
  // The editor ships with the debugger it runs programs under (one release per host)
  LSpec.Debugger := true;
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoCommand(CLICommand.Help, ADAM_CLI_HELP, CLIPositional.Topic, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_COMMAND,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_HELP);
  DoAddString(LSpec.Examples, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXAMPLE_HELP);
  DoAddCommand(LTable, LSpec);

  return LTable;
end;

// An option that belongs to every command until commands are added to it
func DoOption(const AId: CLIOption; const AShort: string; const ALong: string;
  const AValue: string; const ASummary: string): OptionSpec;
var
  LSpec: OptionSpec;
begin
  LSpec.Id := AId;
  LSpec.Short := AShort;
  LSpec.Long := ALong;
  LSpec.Value := AValue;
  LSpec.Summary := ASummary;
  setlength(LSpec.Commands, 0);
  LSpec.Debugger := false;
  return LSpec;
end;

// Adds ASpec at the end of ATable
func DoAddOption(var ATable: OptionTable; const ASpec: OptionSpec);
var
  LCount: int64;
begin
  LCount := len(ATable);
  setlength(ATable, LCount + 1);
  ATable[LCount] := ASpec;
end;

// Every option (see the header)
func DoOptionTable(): OptionTable;
var
  LTable: OptionTable;
  LSpec: OptionSpec;
begin
  setlength(LTable, 0);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Output, ADAM_CLI_OUTPUT_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_OUTPUT_LONG,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_DIR, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_OUTPUT);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.CImport);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Target, ADAM_CLI_TARGET_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_TARGET_LONG,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_TARGET, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_TARGET);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Check);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.CImport);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Optimize, ADAM_CLI_OPTIMIZE_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_OPTIMIZE_LONG,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_LEVEL, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_OPTIMIZE);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Check);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Defaults, "", ADAM_CLI_DEFAULTS_LONG, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_DEFAULTS);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Check);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Run, ADAM_CLI_RUN_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_RUN_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_RUN);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Debug, ADAM_CLI_DEBUG_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_DEBUG_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_DEBUG);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  LSpec.Debugger := true;
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.Host, "", ADAM_CLI_HOST_LONG, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_EXE,
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_HOST);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  LSpec.Debugger := true;
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.EmitIR, "", ADAM_CLI_EMIT_IR_LONG, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_EMIT_IR);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.Build);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.EmitPp, "", ADAM_CLI_EMIT_PP_LONG, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_EMIT_PP);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.CImport);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.EmitUnit, "", ADAM_CLI_EMIT_UNIT_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_EMIT_UNIT);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.CImport);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  LSpec := DoOption(CLIOption.EmitLayout, "", ADAM_CLI_EMIT_LAYOUT_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_EMIT_LAYOUT);
  DoAddCommandId(LSpec.Commands, CLICommand.CImport);
  DoAddOption(LTable, LSpec);

  DoAddOption(LTable, DoOption(CLIOption.NoBanner, "", ADAM_CLI_NO_BANNER_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_NO_BANNER));

  DoAddOption(LTable, DoOption(CLIOption.Quiet, ADAM_CLI_QUIET_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_QUIET_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_QUIET));

  // --heap only in a debug adam: a release build tracks no heap (debug-only machinery), so it
  // has no report to print and neither shows nor takes the option
@ifdef DEBUG
  DoAddOption(LTable, DoOption(CLIOption.Heap, "", ADAM_CLI_HEAP_LONG, "", ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_HEAP));
@endif

  DoAddOption(LTable, DoOption(CLIOption.Help, ADAM_CLI_HELP_SHORT, ADAM_CLI_HELP_LONG, "",
    ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_HELP_OPTION));

  return LTable;
end;

// True when this adam has a debugger part for its host's programs (Adam.Debug.Targets: the
// win64 host today); what needs one (CommandSpec / OptionSpec.Debugger) is there only then
func DoHostDebugs(): bool;
begin
  return DebugTargetFor(DefaultTriple()) <> nil;
end;

// The commands of ATable this host has (AHere), else the ones it lacks: the help and the
// reader take the first, the second only to say a lacking one is not available here (CL0033)
func DoHostCommands(const ATable: CommandTable; const AHere: bool): CommandTable;
var
  LTable: CommandTable;
  LDebugs: bool;
  LI: int64;
begin
  setlength(LTable, 0);
  LDebugs := DoHostDebugs();
  for LI := 0 to len(ATable) - 1 do
    if ((not ATable[LI].Debugger) or LDebugs) = AHere then
      DoAddCommand(LTable, ATable[LI]);
    end;
  end;
  return LTable;
end;

// The options of ATable this host has (AHere), else the ones it lacks, as DoHostCommands
func DoHostOptions(const ATable: OptionTable; const AHere: bool): OptionTable;
var
  LTable: OptionTable;
  LDebugs: bool;
  LI: int64;
begin
  setlength(LTable, 0);
  LDebugs := DoHostDebugs();
  for LI := 0 to len(ATable) - 1 do
    if ((not ATable[LI].Debugger) or LDebugs) = AHere then
      DoAddOption(LTable, ATable[LI]);
    end;
  end;
  return LTable;
end;

// The index of the command whose word is AWord in ATable; -1 when there is none
func DoFindCommand(const ATable: CommandTable; const AWord: string): int64;
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  for LI := 0 to len(ATable) - 1 do
    if ATable[LI].Word = AWord then
      return LI;
    end;
  end;
  return -1;
end;

// The index of the option written AArg (its short or its long form) in ATable; -1 when there
// is none
func DoFindOption(const ATable: OptionTable; const AArg: string): int64;
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  for LI := 0 to len(ATable) - 1 do
    if (ATable[LI].Long = AArg) or ((ATable[LI].Short <> "") and (ATable[LI].Short = AArg)) then
      return LI;
    end;
  end;
  return -1;
end;

// True when AArg is written as an option: it starts with '-'
func DoIsOption(const AArg: string): bool;
begin
  if len(AArg) = 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  return AArg[0] = '-';
end;

// True when AOption belongs to ACommand (an option that lists no command belongs to every one)
func DoBelongs(const AOption: OptionSpec; const ACommand: CLICommand): bool;
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  if len(AOption.Commands) = 0 then
    return true;
  end;
  for LI := 0 to len(AOption.Commands) - 1 do
    if AOption.Commands[LI] = ACommand then
      return true;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

// True when AOption belongs to every command
func DoBelongsToAll(const AOption: OptionSpec): bool;
begin
  return len(AOption.Commands) = 0;
end;

// The index in argv of the first '--' (what ends adam's own arguments); 0 when the line has
// none
func DoSeparatorAt(): int32;
var
  LIndex: int32;
begin
  for LIndex := 1 to paramcount() do
    if paramstr(LIndex) = ADAM_CLI_ARGS_SEPARATOR then
      return LIndex;
    end;
  end;
  return 0;
end;

// The last index in argv adam reads as its own: the one before '--', else the last
func DoLastArg(): int32;
var
  LSeparator: int32;
begin
  LSeparator := DoSeparatorAt();
  if LSeparator > 0 then
    return LSeparator - 1;
  end;
  return paramcount();
end;

// The index in argv of the command: the first argument that is neither an option nor a
// value-taking option's value. 0 when the line has none
func DoCommandAt(const AOptions: OptionTable): int32;
var
  LIndex: int32;
  LArg: string;
  LOption: int64;
begin
  LIndex := 1;
  while LIndex <= DoLastArg() do
    LArg := paramstr(LIndex);
    if not DoIsOption(LArg) then
      return LIndex;
    end;
    LOption := DoFindOption(AOptions, LArg);
    // An option taking a value skips it, and so does the hidden --dev-pack (its spec)
    if ((LOption >= 0) and (AOptions[LOption].Value <> "")) or
      (LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_PACK_LONG) then
      LIndex := LIndex + 2;
    else
      LIndex := LIndex + 1;
    end;
  end;
  return 0;
end;

// True when the line gives --no-banner or --quiet as an option (never as another option's
// value), read before the line is checked so the banner leads even a mistake's line
func DoWantsNoBanner(const AOptions: OptionTable): bool;
var
  LIndex: int32;
  LOption: int64;
begin
  // dap, lsp: stdout is the protocol; info: stdout is its JSON; editor: the editor runs on its
  // own, adam returns at once (pcpp's)
  LIndex := DoCommandAt(AOptions);
  if (LIndex > 0) and ((paramstr(LIndex) = ADAM_CLI_DAP) or (paramstr(LIndex) = ADAM_CLI_LSP) or
    (paramstr(LIndex) = ADAM_CLI_INFO) or (paramstr(LIndex) = ADAM_CLI_EDITOR)) then
    return true;
  end;
  LIndex := 1;
  while LIndex <= DoLastArg() do
    LOption := DoFindOption(AOptions, paramstr(LIndex));
    if LOption < 0 then
      LIndex := LIndex + 1;
    else
      // --quiet prints no banner either
      if (AOptions[LOption].Id = CLIOption.NoBanner) or (AOptions[LOption].Id = CLIOption.Quiet) then
        return true;
      end;
      if AOptions[LOption].Value <> "" then
        LIndex := LIndex + 2;
      else
        LIndex := LIndex + 1;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

// The help a mistake points to: `adam help <command>` for the command at ACommand in ACommands,
// `adam help` when ACommand is -1
func DoSee(const ACommands: CommandTable; const ACommand: int64): string;
begin
  if ACommand < 0 then
    return ADAM_MSG_CLI_SEE_ANY;
  end;
  return NoArgs().Str(ACommands[ACommand].Word).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_SEE);
end;

// Reports one command line mistake into AReports: an Error with no place, ACode, ATemplate
// filled with AArgs
func DoReport(const AReports: ref Diagnostics; const ACode: string; const ATemplate: string;
  const AArgs: MessageArgs);
begin
  AReports.Add(Severity.Error, ACode, NoPlace(), ATemplate, AArgs);
end;

// DoReport, then false: what a reader returns on a mistake
func DoMistake(const AReports: ref Diagnostics; const ACode: string; const ATemplate: string;
  const AArgs: MessageArgs): bool;
begin
  DoReport(AReports, ACode, ATemplate, AArgs);
  return false;
end;

// The target -t gave (ARequest.TargetText, a triple) checked against the registry, put into
// ARequest.TargetTriple; nothing given: nothing to check. ASee names the help in a mistake.
// A triple the registry lacks: reported (CL0009, naming every triple it has), false
func DoReadTarget(const AReports: ref Diagnostics; var ARequest: CLIRequest;
  const ASee: string): bool;
var
  LTarget: ref Target;
begin
  if ARequest.TargetText = "" then
    return true;
  end;
  LTarget := FindTarget(ARequest.TargetText);
  if LTarget = nil then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_009, ADAM_MSG_CLI_BAD_TARGET,
      NoArgs().Str(ARequest.TargetText).Str(KnownTriples()).Str(ASee));
  end;
  ARequest.TargetTriple := LTarget.Triple();
  return true;
end;

// The level -opt gave (ARequest.LevelText, exact case) into ARequest.Level and LevelGiven;
// nothing given: nothing to check. ASee names the help in a mistake. No level's name:
// reported (CL0020, a retired spelling naming its new one), false
func DoReadLevel(const AReports: ref Diagnostics; var ARequest: CLIRequest;
  const ASee: string): bool;
var
  LLevel: OptLevel;
begin
  if ARequest.LevelText = "" then
    return true;
  end;
  LLevel := OptLevel.Debug;
  if OptLevelOfName(ARequest.LevelText, LLevel) then
    ARequest.Level := LLevel;
    ARequest.LevelGiven := true;
    return true;
  end;
  if OptLevelOfRetiredName(ARequest.LevelText, LLevel) then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_020, ADAM_MSG_CLI_RETIRED_LEVEL,
      NoArgs().Str(ARequest.LevelText).Str(OptLevelName(LLevel)).Str(ASee));
  end;
  return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_020, ADAM_MSG_CLI_BAD_LEVEL,
    NoArgs().Str(ARequest.LevelText).Str(OptLevelNames()).Str(ASee));
end;

// Option AId's handler: AValue (the argument after a value-taking option, else "") put into
// ARequest
func DoApply(var ARequest: CLIRequest; const AId: CLIOption; const AValue: string);
begin
  if AId = CLIOption.Output then
    ARequest.Output := AValue;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Target then
    ARequest.TargetText := AValue;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Optimize then
    ARequest.LevelText := AValue;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Defaults then
    ARequest.Defaults := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Run then
    ARequest.Run := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Debug then
    ARequest.Debug := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Host then
    ARequest.HostPath := AValue;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.EmitIR then
    ARequest.EmitIR := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.EmitPp then
    ARequest.EmitPp := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.EmitUnit then
    ARequest.EmitUnit := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.EmitLayout then
    ARequest.EmitLayout := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.NoBanner then
    ARequest.NoBanner := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Quiet then
    ARequest.Quiet := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Heap then
    ARequest.Heap := true;
  end;
  if AId = CLIOption.Help then
    ARequest.WantHelp := true;
  end;
end;

// Reads the option at AIndex (written as an option) into ARequest and moves AIndex past it
// (and its value). ACommandWord / ASee name the command given (else adam) and its help in a
// mistake; ASeen holds the options already given. A mistake: reported, false
func DoReadOption(const ACommands: CommandTable; const AOptions: OptionTable;
  const AAbsent: OptionTable; const AReports: ref Diagnostics; var ARequest: CLIRequest; const ACommandWord: string;
  const ASee: string; var ASeen: BoolArray; var AIndex: int32): bool;
var
  LArg: string;
  LOption: int64;
  LBelongs: bool;
  LValue: string;
begin
  LArg := paramstr(AIndex);
  LOption := DoFindOption(AOptions, LArg);
  LBelongs := false;
  if LOption >= 0 then
    if ARequest.Command >= 0 then
      LBelongs := DoBelongs(AOptions[LOption], ACommands[ARequest.Command].Id);
    else
      LBelongs := DoBelongsToAll(AOptions[LOption]);
    end;
  end;
  // An option this host lacks (AAbsent: its debugger's) is said to be so, not unknown
  if (LOption < 0) and (DoFindOption(AAbsent, LArg) >= 0) then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_033, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NOT_ON_HOST,
      NoArgs().Str(LArg).Str(DefaultTriple()));
  end;
  if not LBelongs then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_005, ADAM_MSG_CLI_UNKNOWN_OPTION,
      NoArgs().Str(LArg).Str(ACommandWord).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if ASeen[LOption] then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_008, ADAM_MSG_CLI_OPTION_TWICE,
      NoArgs().Str(LArg).Str(ASee));
  end;
  ASeen[LOption] := true;
  LValue := "";
  if AOptions[LOption].Value <> "" then
    // A value-taking option takes the next argument, whatever it is (never '--')
    if AIndex = DoLastArg() then
      return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_007, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NO_VALUE,
        NoArgs().Str(LArg).Str(AOptions[LOption].Value).Str(ASee));
    end;
    LValue := paramstr(AIndex + 1);
    AIndex := AIndex + 2;
  else
    AIndex := AIndex + 1;
  end;
  DoApply(ARequest, AOptions[LOption].Id, LValue);
  return true;
end;

// The arguments after '--' into ARequest.RunArgs, as given: they are the program's (-r or
// -d), so '--' without either is a mistake (CL0010, ASee the help to see); -r with -d is one
// too (CL0026: both run it). A mistake: reported, false
func DoReadRunArgs(const AReports: ref Diagnostics; var ARequest: CLIRequest;
  const ASee: string): bool;
var
  LSeparator: int32;
  LIndex: int32;
begin
  if ARequest.Run and ARequest.Debug then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_026, ADAM_MSG_CLI_RUN_AND_DEBUG,
      NoArgs().Str(ASee));
  end;
  if (len(ARequest.HostPath) > 0) and not ARequest.Debug then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_028, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HOST_WITHOUT_DEBUG,
      NoArgs().Str(ASee));
  end;
  LSeparator := DoSeparatorAt();
  if LSeparator = 0 then
    return true;
  end;
  if not (ARequest.Run or ARequest.Debug) then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_010, ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARGS_WITHOUT_RUN,
      NoArgs().Str(ASee));
  end;
  for LIndex := LSeparator + 1 to paramcount() do
    DoAddString(ARequest.RunArgs, paramstr(LIndex));
  end;
  return true;
end;

// True when the command ARequest names takes two positional arguments (init)
func DoTakesTwo(const ACommands: CommandTable; const ARequest: CLIRequest): bool;
begin
  if ARequest.Command < 0 then
    return false;
  end;
  return ACommands[ARequest.Command].Positional = CLIPositional.NewProject;
end;

// Takes AArg as the command's next positional argument: the first is Positional, init's
// second its TypeText. One more than the command takes: CL0004, reported, false
func DoAddPositional(const ACommands: CommandTable; const AReports: ref Diagnostics;
  var ARequest: CLIRequest; const ACommandWord: string; const ASee: string;
  const AArg: string): bool;
begin
  if ACommands[ARequest.Command].Positional = CLIPositional.None then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_027, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NO_ARGUMENT,
      NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(AArg).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if ACommands[ARequest.Command].Positional = CLIPositional.Files then
    setlength(ARequest.Files, len(ARequest.Files) + 1);
    ARequest.Files[len(ARequest.Files) - 1] := AArg;
    return true;
  end;
  if ARequest.Positional = "" then
    ARequest.Positional := AArg;
    return true;
  end;
  if not DoTakesTwo(ACommands, ARequest) then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_004, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXTRA_ARG,
      NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(AArg).Str(ARequest.Positional).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if ARequest.TypeText = "" then
    ARequest.TypeText := AArg;
    return true;
  end;
  return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_004, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EXTRA_ARG_TWO,
    NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(AArg).Str(ARequest.TypeText).Str(ASee));
end;

// The command's positional arguments, once all are read: a file the command needs (CL0003),
// cimport's spec (CL0024), init's name and type both given (CL0015) and the type exe, dll or
// lib (CL0016). A mistake: reported, false
func DoCheckPositionals(const ACommands: CommandTable; const AReports: ref Diagnostics;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest; const ACommandWord: string; const ASee: string): bool;
var
  LKind: ModuleKind;
begin
  if (ACommands[ARequest.Command].Positional = CLIPositional.File) and
    (ARequest.Positional = "") then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_003, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NO_FILE,
      NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(ACommandWord).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if (ACommands[ARequest.Command].Positional = CLIPositional.Spec) and
    (ARequest.Positional = "") then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_024, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NO_SPEC,
      NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(ACommandWord).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if not DoTakesTwo(ACommands, ARequest) then
    return true;
  end;
  if ARequest.TypeText = "" then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_015, ADAM_MSG_CLI_INIT_ARGS,
      NoArgs().Str(ACommandWord).Str(ACommandWord).Str(ASee));
  end;
  if not ProjectKindFromText(ARequest.TypeText, LKind) then
    return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_016, ADAM_MSG_CLI_INIT_BAD_TYPE,
      NoArgs().Str(ARequest.TypeText).Str(ASee));
  end;
  return true;
end;

// Reads the whole command line into ARequest (see the header). A mistake: reported into
// AReports, false
func DoRead(const ACommands: CommandTable; const AOptions: OptionTable;
  const AAbsentCommands: CommandTable; const AAbsentOptions: OptionTable;
  const AReports: ref Diagnostics; var ARequest: CLIRequest): bool;
var
  LCommandAt: int32;
  LCommandWord: string;
  LSee: string;
  LSeen: BoolArray;
  LIndex: int32;
  LArg: string;
  LI: int64;
begin
  ARequest.Command := -1;
  ARequest.Positional := "";
  ARequest.TypeText := "";
  setlength(ARequest.Files, 0);
  ARequest.Output := "";
  ARequest.TargetText := "";
  ARequest.TargetTriple := "";
  ARequest.LevelText := "";
  ARequest.Level := OptLevel.Debug;
  ARequest.LevelGiven := false;
  ARequest.Defaults := false;
  ARequest.Run := false;
  ARequest.Debug := false;
  setlength(ARequest.RunArgs, 0);
  ARequest.EmitIR := false;
  ARequest.EmitPp := false;
  ARequest.EmitUnit := false;
  ARequest.EmitLayout := false;
  ARequest.NoBanner := false;
  ARequest.Quiet := false;
  ARequest.Heap := false;
  ARequest.WantHelp := false;
  ARequest.SelfBuild := false;
  ARequest.DevEditor := false;
  ARequest.DevBuildAdam := false;
  ARequest.DevPack := false;
  ARequest.DevPackSpec := "";

  // The command first: what every option and argument after it is checked against
  LCommandAt := DoCommandAt(AOptions);
  LCommandWord := ADAM_CLI_PROGRAM;
  if LCommandAt > 0 then
    ARequest.Command := DoFindCommand(ACommands, paramstr(LCommandAt));
    // A command this host lacks (AAbsentCommands: its debugger's) is said to be so, not unknown
    if (ARequest.Command < 0) and (DoFindCommand(AAbsentCommands, paramstr(LCommandAt)) >= 0) then
      return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_033, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NOT_ON_HOST,
        NoArgs().Str(paramstr(LCommandAt)).Str(DefaultTriple()));
    end;
    if ARequest.Command < 0 then
      return DoMistake(AReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_002, ADAM_MSG_CLI_UNKNOWN_COMMAND,
        NoArgs().Str(paramstr(LCommandAt)));
    end;
    LCommandWord := ACommands[ARequest.Command].Word;
  end;
  LSee := DoSee(ACommands, ARequest.Command);

  setlength(LSeen, len(AOptions));
  for LI := 0 to len(LSeen) - 1 do
    LSeen[LI] := false;
  end;
  LIndex := 1;
  while LIndex <= DoLastArg() do
    LArg := paramstr(LIndex);
    if (LIndex = LCommandAt) or (LArg = ADAM_CLI_SELF_BUILD_LONG) or
      (LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_EDITOR_LONG) or (LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_BUILD_ADAM_LONG) or
      (LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_PACK_LONG) then
      // the hidden switches are taken here, before the option table (which never shows them)
      if LArg = ADAM_CLI_SELF_BUILD_LONG then
        ARequest.SelfBuild := true;
      end;
      if LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_EDITOR_LONG then
        ARequest.DevEditor := true;
      end;
      if LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_BUILD_ADAM_LONG then
        ARequest.DevBuildAdam := true;
      end;
      // --dev-pack takes the argument after it as its spec (none there: DevPack says so)
      if LArg = ADAM_CLI_DEV_PACK_LONG then
        ARequest.DevPack := true;
        if LIndex < DoLastArg() then
          LIndex := LIndex + 1;
          ARequest.DevPackSpec := paramstr(LIndex);
        end;
      end;
      LIndex := LIndex + 1;
    else
      if DoIsOption(LArg) then
        if not DoReadOption(ACommands, AOptions, AAbsentOptions, AReports, ARequest, LCommandWord,
          LSee, LSeen,
          LIndex) then
          return false;
        end;
      else
        // Every argument after the command that is no option is a positional argument
        if not DoAddPositional(ACommands, AReports, ARequest, LCommandWord, LSee, LArg) then
          return false;
        end;
        LIndex := LIndex + 1;
      end;
    end;
  end;

  if (ARequest.Command >= 0) and not ARequest.WantHelp then
    if not DoCheckPositionals(ACommands, AReports, ARequest, LCommandWord, LSee) then
      return false;
    end;
  end;
  if not DoReadRunArgs(AReports, ARequest, LSee) then
    return false;
  end;
  if not DoReadLevel(AReports, ARequest, LSee) then
    return false;
  end;
  return DoReadTarget(AReports, ARequest, LSee);
end;

// AText with blanks after it up to AWidth bytes (every help text is ASCII, so a byte is a
// column); AText itself when it is that wide already
func DoPad(const AText: string; const AWidth: int64): string;
begin
  if len(AText) >= AWidth then
    return AText;
  end;
  return AText + StringOfChar(' ', AWidth - len(AText));
end;

// The wider of AWidth and AOther: a help column grows to its widest entry
func DoWider(const AWidth: int64; const AOther: int64): int64;
begin
  if AOther > AWidth then
    return AOther;
  end;
  return AWidth;
end;

type
  // Where the banner and the help go: stdout, in color on a console that takes VT sequences
  // (headings bold, the left column's names and the examples cyan, placeholders green, the
  // link yellow: Adam.Core.Common's sequences), plain when piped or redirected. Every column
  // is padded before it is colored, so a colored help lines up as a plain one
  HelpOut = object
    hidden FColor: bool;

    init(const AColor: bool);
    begin
      self.FColor := AColor;
    end;

    // AText in the VT color AColor when this output takes color, else AText itself
    hidden const method DoPaint(const AText: string; const AColor: string): string;
    begin
      if not self.FColor or (AText = "") then
        return AText;
      end;
      return AColor + AText + ADAM_COLOR_RESET;
    end;

    // Prints AText as one line
    const method Line(const AText: string);
    begin
      println("{}", AText);
    end;

    // Prints a heading (a section's name, the banner) as one line
    const method Heading(const AText: string);
    begin
      self.Line(self.DoPaint(AText, ADAM_COLOR_BOLD));
    end;

    // Prints AText (a link) as one line
    const method Link(const AText: string);
    begin
      self.Line(self.DoPaint(AText, ADAM_COLOR_YELLOW));
    end;

    // APlaceholder (what the user types in its place: <file>, [options]) in its own color
    const method Placeholder(const APlaceholder: string): string;
    begin
      return self.DoPaint(APlaceholder, ADAM_COLOR_GREEN);
    end;

    // Prints one row: AName in a column ANameWidth wide and APlaceholder after it ("" = none:
    // AName alone), the two together padded to AWidth, then ARight; with no ARight the row
    // ends at its left side's last character (no trailing blanks)
    const method Row(const AName: string; const ANameWidth: int64; const APlaceholder: string;
      const AWidth: int64; const ARight: string);
    begin
      if ARight = "" then
        if APlaceholder = "" then
          self.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + self.DoPaint(AName, ADAM_COLOR_CYAN));
        else
          self.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + self.DoPaint(DoPad(AName, ANameWidth), ADAM_COLOR_CYAN) +
            " " + self.Placeholder(APlaceholder));
        end;
        return;
      end;
      if APlaceholder = "" then
        self.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + self.DoPaint(DoPad(AName, AWidth), ADAM_COLOR_CYAN) +
          ADAM_CLI_GAP + ARight);
      else
        self.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + self.DoPaint(DoPad(AName, ANameWidth), ADAM_COLOR_CYAN) + " " +
          self.Placeholder(DoPad(APlaceholder, AWidth - ANameWidth - 1)) + ADAM_CLI_GAP + ARight);
      end;
    end;

    // Prints one example command line, indented
    const method Example(const AText: string);
    begin
      self.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + self.DoPaint(AText, ADAM_COLOR_CYAN));
    end;
  end;

// The width a row's left side takes: AName, then APlaceholder after a column ANameWidth wide
// ("" = none: AName alone)
func DoLeftWidth(const AName: string; const ANameWidth: int64; const APlaceholder: string): int64;
begin
  if APlaceholder = "" then
    return len(AName);
  end;
  return DoWider(ANameWidth, len(AName)) + 1 + len(APlaceholder);
end;

// An option's name in the help: its short form (when it has one), then its long form
func DoOptionFlags(const ASpec: OptionSpec): string;
begin
  if ASpec.Short <> "" then
    return ASpec.Short + ", " + ASpec.Long;
  end;
  return ASpec.Long;
end;

// The word of the command AId in ACommands
func DoCommandWord(const ACommands: CommandTable; const AId: CLICommand): string;
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  for LI := 0 to len(ACommands) - 1 do
    if ACommands[LI].Id = AId then
      return ACommands[LI].Word;
    end;
  end;
  return "";
end;

// An option's right column in adam's own help: its summary, and the commands it belongs to
// when it does not belong to every one
func DoOptionRightAll(const ACommands: CommandTable; const ASpec: OptionSpec): string;
var
  LWords: StringArray;
  LI: int64;
begin
  if DoBelongsToAll(ASpec) then
    return ASpec.Summary;
  end;
  setlength(LWords, 0);
  for LI := 0 to len(ASpec.Commands) - 1 do
    DoAddString(LWords, DoCommandWord(ACommands, ASpec.Commands[LI]));
  end;
  return NoArgs().Str(ASpec.Summary).Str(JoinStrings(LWords, ", ")).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_ONLY_FOR);
end;

// The banner into AOut: adam's name and version, its copyright, its link (Adam.Core.Common's
// identity), a blank line after it
func DoBanner(const AOut: ref HelpOut);
begin
  AOut.Heading(NoArgs().Str(ADAM_PRODUCT_NAME).Str(AdamVersionText()).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_BANNER));
  AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ADAM_COPYRIGHT).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_BANNER_COPYRIGHT));
  AOut.Link(ADAM_URL);
  AOut.Line("");
end;

// Prints into AOut the examples of every command in ACommands from AFirst to ALast, under
// their heading (nothing when there are none)
func DoPrintExamples(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACommands: CommandTable;
  const AFirst: int64; const ALast: int64);
var
  LI: int64;
  LJ: int64;
  LAny: bool;
begin
  LAny := false;
  for LI := AFirst to ALast do
    for LJ := 0 to len(ACommands[LI].Examples) - 1 do
      if not LAny then
        AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_EXAMPLES);
        LAny := true;
      end;
      AOut.Example(ACommands[LI].Examples[LJ]);
    end;
  end;
  if LAny then
    AOut.Line("");
  end;
end;

// The width of the widest target triple the registry has
func DoTargetsWidth(): int64;
var
  LTargets: TargetList;
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LTargets := AllTargets();
  LWidth := 0;
  for LI := 0 to len(LTargets) - 1 do
    LWidth := DoWider(LWidth, len(LTargets[LI].Triple()));
  end;
  return LWidth;
end;

// Prints into AOut every target the registry has under its heading, its triple in a left
// column AWidth wide, the default one marked beside it, a blank line after
func DoPrintTargets(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const AWidth: int64);
var
  LTargets: TargetList;
  LI: int64;
  LMark: string;
begin
  LTargets := AllTargets();
  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_TARGETS);
  for LI := 0 to len(LTargets) - 1 do
    LMark := "";
    if LTargets[LI].IsDefault() then
      LMark := NoArgs().Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_TARGET_DEFAULT);
    end;
    AOut.Row(LTargets[LI].Triple(), 0, "", AWidth, LMark);
  end;
  AOut.Line("");
end;

// True when the command ACommand takes the option that names a target (its help then lists
// the targets)
func DoTakesTarget(const AOptions: OptionTable; const ACommand: CLICommand): bool;
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  for LI := 0 to len(AOptions) - 1 do
    if (AOptions[LI].Id = CLIOption.Target) and DoBelongs(AOptions[LI], ACommand) then
      return true;
    end;
  end;
  return false;
end;

// True when the help being printed lists AOption: adam's own help (AAll) lists every option,
// a command's help the ones that belong to ACommand
func DoListed(const AOption: OptionSpec; const AAll: bool; const ACommand: CLICommand): bool;
begin
  return AAll or DoBelongs(AOption, ACommand);
end;

// The width of the widest command word in ACommands: the column their arguments line up after
func DoWordWidth(const ACommands: CommandTable): int64;
var
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LWidth := 0;
  for LI := 0 to len(ACommands) - 1 do
    LWidth := DoWider(LWidth, len(ACommands[LI].Word));
  end;
  return LWidth;
end;

// The width of the widest flags of the options listed (DoListed): the column their values
// line up after
func DoFlagWidth(const AOptions: OptionTable; const AAll: bool; const ACommand: CLICommand): int64;
var
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LWidth := 0;
  for LI := 0 to len(AOptions) - 1 do
    if DoListed(AOptions[LI], AAll, ACommand) then
      LWidth := DoWider(LWidth, len(DoOptionFlags(AOptions[LI])));
    end;
  end;
  return LWidth;
end;

// AWidth grown to the widest left side of the options listed (DoListed), their values after a
// flag column AFlagWidth wide
func DoOptionsWidth(const AOptions: OptionTable; const AAll: bool; const ACommand: CLICommand;
  const AFlagWidth: int64; const AWidth: int64): int64;
var
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LWidth := AWidth;
  for LI := 0 to len(AOptions) - 1 do
    if DoListed(AOptions[LI], AAll, ACommand) then
      LWidth := DoWider(LWidth, DoLeftWidth(DoOptionFlags(AOptions[LI]), AFlagWidth,
        AOptions[LI].Value));
    end;
  end;
  return LWidth;
end;

// adam's own help into AOut: the usage, every command, every option, every target, every
// example
func DoHelpAll(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACommands: CommandTable;
  const AOptions: OptionTable);
var
  LWordWidth: int64;
  LFlagWidth: int64;
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  // Words and flags each in a column of their own, their placeholders lined up after it; one
  // left column for every list, as wide as its widest entry (CLICommand.Help: AAll ignores it)
  LWordWidth := DoWordWidth(ACommands);
  LFlagWidth := DoFlagWidth(AOptions, true, CLICommand.Help);
  LWidth := DoTargetsWidth();
  for LI := 0 to len(ACommands) - 1 do
    LWidth := DoWider(LWidth, DoLeftWidth(ACommands[LI].Word, LWordWidth, ACommands[LI].Argument));
  end;
  LWidth := DoOptionsWidth(AOptions, true, CLICommand.Help, LFlagWidth, LWidth);

  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_USAGE);
  AOut.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + NoArgs().Str(AOut.Placeholder(ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_ANY_COMMAND))
    .Str(AOut.Placeholder(ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_OPTIONS)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_USAGE_ANY));
  AOut.Line("");
  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_COMMANDS);
  for LI := 0 to len(ACommands) - 1 do
    AOut.Row(ACommands[LI].Word, LWordWidth, ACommands[LI].Argument, LWidth,
      ACommands[LI].Summary);
  end;
  AOut.Line("");
  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_OPTIONS);
  for LI := 0 to len(AOptions) - 1 do
    AOut.Row(DoOptionFlags(AOptions[LI]), LFlagWidth, AOptions[LI].Value, LWidth,
      DoOptionRightAll(ACommands, AOptions[LI]));
  end;
  AOut.Line("");
  DoPrintTargets(AOut, LWidth);
  DoPrintExamples(AOut, ACommands, 0, len(ACommands) - 1);
  AOut.Line(ADAM_MSG_CLI_MORE);
end;

// The help of the command at ACommand into AOut: its usage, its summary, its options, the
// targets (when it takes -t), its examples
func DoHelpCommand(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACommands: CommandTable;
  const AOptions: OptionTable; const ACommand: int64);
var
  LSpec: CommandSpec;
  LFlagWidth: int64;
  LWidth: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LSpec := ACommands[ACommand];
  LWidth := 0;
  if DoTakesTarget(AOptions, LSpec.Id) then
    LWidth := DoTargetsWidth();
  end;
  LFlagWidth := DoFlagWidth(AOptions, false, LSpec.Id);
  LWidth := DoOptionsWidth(AOptions, false, LSpec.Id, LFlagWidth, LWidth);

  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_USAGE);
  if LSpec.Argument = "" then
    AOut.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + NoArgs().Str(LSpec.Word)
      .Str(AOut.Placeholder(ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_OPTIONS)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_USAGE_COMMAND));
  else
    AOut.Line(ADAM_CLI_INDENT + NoArgs().Str(LSpec.Word).Str(AOut.Placeholder(LSpec.Argument))
      .Str(AOut.Placeholder(ADAM_MSG_CLI_ARG_OPTIONS)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_USAGE_COMMAND_ARG));
  end;
  AOut.Line("");
  AOut.Line(LSpec.Summary);
  AOut.Line("");
  AOut.Heading(ADAM_MSG_CLI_HEAD_OPTIONS);
  for LI := 0 to len(AOptions) - 1 do
    if DoBelongs(AOptions[LI], LSpec.Id) then
      AOut.Row(DoOptionFlags(AOptions[LI]), LFlagWidth, AOptions[LI].Value, LWidth,
        AOptions[LI].Summary);
    end;
  end;
  AOut.Line("");
  if DoTakesTarget(AOptions, LSpec.Id) then
    DoPrintTargets(AOut, LWidth);
  end;
  DoPrintExamples(AOut, ACommands, ACommand, ACommand);
end;

// The Parse phase line: AParsed units parsed from source (ALines their lines) and AFromACU
// taken from their .acu, as the tree counted them (Compiler's PhaseEnded). With none from .acu
// (a cold build) the plain form; else the parsed and the loaded apart, so the counts agree
// ("Parsed 1 unit (232 lines), 72 from .acu in 0.57s"); one unit is named in the singular
func DoParseText(const AParsed: int64; const ALines: int64; const AFromACU: int64;
  const ASeconds: string): string;
begin
  if AFromACU = 0 then
    if AParsed = 1 then
      return NoArgs().Int(ALines).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_PARSE_ONE);
    end;
    return NoArgs().Int(AParsed).Int(ALines).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_PARSE);
  end;
  if AParsed = 1 then
    return NoArgs().Int(ALines).Int(AFromACU).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_PARSE_ACU_ONE);
  end;
  return NoArgs().Int(AParsed).Int(ALines).Int(AFromACU).Str(ASeconds)
    .Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_PARSE_ACU);
end;

// AMilliseconds as seconds with two decimals, rounded down ("0.42", "12.05")
func DoSeconds(const AMilliseconds: int64): string;
var
  LHundredths: int64;
  LFraction: string;
begin
  LHundredths := (AMilliseconds mod 1000) div 10;
  LFraction := IntToStr(LHundredths);
  if LHundredths < 10 then
    LFraction := "0" + LFraction;
  end;
  return IntToStr(AMilliseconds div 1000) + "." + LFraction;
end;

var
  // Set as the process ends (DoLiveQuit, an exit handler): a ticker still running stops at its
  // next wake and draws nothing more, so an exit (Halt) never waits on it
  GLiveQuit: int32;

// The exit handler CLIPhases registers when it draws live: the ticker's stop at any exit
func DoLiveQuit();
begin
  atomicstore(GLiveQuit, 1);
end;

type
  // The phase lines: one line per phase as it ends, printed into an output with the time
  // since the phase before it ended (the first: since the listener was made). On a console
  // that takes VT sequences (Live) the running phase's line is drawn in place too: its text
  // (the phase, the unit and step it is at) and its whole seconds, redrawn as each step
  // starts and each second (Tick, a ticker task's), overwritten by the final line. Every
  // write to the screen is made holding FLine, so the ticker and the compile never mix
  CLIPhases = object(PhaseListener)
    hidden FOut: ref HelpOut;
    hidden FLast: int64;
    hidden FLive: bool;
    hidden FLine: mutex;
    // The running phase's live text ("" while none runs), whether a live line is on the
    // screen, and whether the compile is over (Finish: nothing is drawn after it)
    hidden FText: string;
    hidden FShown: bool;
    hidden FDone: bool;
    // Held by the compile while it runs (DoCompileLive): the ticker sleeps on it and stops
    // once it is free
    Hold: mutex;

    init(const AOut: ref HelpOut);
    begin
      self.FOut := AOut;
      self.FLast := TickCountMs();
      self.FLive := EscapesEnabled();
      self.FText := "";
      self.FShown := false;
      self.FDone := false;
      if self.FLive then
        AtExit(DoLiveQuit);
      end;
    end;

    // True when the running phase is drawn in place (a console that takes VT sequences)
    const method Live(): bool;
    begin
      return self.FLive;
    end;

    // The phase line's arguments before its seconds, filled into its template
    hidden const method DoText(const APhase: BuildPhase; const AFirst: int64;
      const ASecond: int64; const AThird: int64; const AText: string;
      const ASeconds: string): string;
    begin
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Parse then
        return DoParseText(AFirst, ASecond, AThird, ASeconds);
      end;
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Analyze then
        return NoArgs().Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_ANALYZE);
      end;
      // AFirst units lowered (one named in the singular), ASecond routines
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Lower then
        if AFirst = 1 then
          return NoArgs().Int(ASecond).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_LOWER_ONE);
        end;
        return NoArgs().Int(AFirst).Int(ASecond).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_LOWER);
      end;
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Generate then
        return NoArgs().Int(AFirst).Str(ASeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_GENERATE);
      end;
      // BuildPhase.Link
      return NoArgs().Str(ExtractFileName(AText)).Int(AFirst).Str(ASeconds)
        .Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PHASE_LINK);
    end;

    // The running phase's own word (Parsing, Analyzing ...)
    hidden const method DoLiveWord(const APhase: BuildPhase): string;
    begin
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Parse then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_PARSE;
      end;
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Analyze then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_ANALYZE;
      end;
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Lower then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_LOWER;
      end;
      if APhase = BuildPhase.Generate then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_GENERATE;
      end;
      return ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_LINK;
    end;

    // A unit step's own word (lower, optimize, generate, write)
    hidden const method DoStepWord(const AStep: BuildStep): string;
    begin
      if AStep = BuildStep.Lower then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_STEP_LOWER;
      end;
      if AStep = BuildStep.Optimize then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_STEP_OPTIMIZE;
      end;
      if AStep = BuildStep.Generate then
        return ADAM_MSG_CLI_STEP_GENERATE;
      end;
      return ADAM_MSG_CLI_STEP_WRITE;
    end;

    // AText cut to the terminal's width less one column (by display columns), so the live
    // line never wraps: a wrapped line is not redrawn in place
    hidden const method DoFit(const AText: string): string;
    var
      LLimit: int64;
      LColumns: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LStart: int64;
    begin
      LLimit := int64(GetTerminalWidth()) - 1;
      if DisplayWidth(AText) <= LLimit then
        return AText;
      end;
      LColumns := 0;
      LIndex := 0;
      while LIndex < len(AText) do
        LStart := LIndex;
        DecodeUTF8Char(AText, LIndex);
        LColumns := LColumns + DisplayWidth(Substring(AText, LStart, LIndex - LStart));
        if LColumns > LLimit then
          return Substring(AText, 0, LStart);
        end;
      end;
      return AText;
    end;

    // The live line drawn again (its text and the whole seconds since its phase started) in
    // place of the one on the screen; held FLine is the caller's
    hidden method DoDraw();
    var
      LSeconds: int64;
    begin
      if (self.FText = "") or self.FDone or (atomicload(GLiveQuit) <> 0) then
        return;
      end;
      LSeconds := (TickCountMs() - self.FLast) div 1000;
      WriteText(CsiCr + CsiClearLine +
        self.DoFit(NoArgs().Str(self.FText).Int(LSeconds).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_LINE)));
      self.FShown := true;
    end;

    // The live line on the screen (if any) erased, the cursor at its start; held FLine is the
    // caller's
    hidden method DoErase();
    begin
      if self.FShown then
        WriteText(CsiCr + CsiClearLine);
        self.FShown := false;
      end;
    end;

    // The live text set to AText and drawn
    hidden method DoShow(const AText: string);
    begin
      lock (self.FLine) do
        self.FText := AText;
        self.DoDraw();
      end;
    end;

    override method PhaseStarted(const APhase: BuildPhase);
    begin
      if self.FLive then
        self.DoShow(self.DoLiveWord(APhase));
      end;
    end;

    override method StepStarted(const APhase: BuildPhase; const AStep: BuildStep;
      const ADone: int64; const ATotal: int64; const AUnit: string);
    var
      LWord: string;
    begin
      if not self.FLive then
        return;
      end;
      LWord := self.DoLiveWord(APhase);
      if AStep = BuildStep.Program then
        self.DoShow(NoArgs().Str(LWord).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_PROGRAM));
        return;
      end;
      if AStep = BuildStep.Merge then
        self.DoShow(NoArgs().Str(LWord).Int(ADone).Int(ATotal).Str(AUnit)
          .Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_MERGE));
        return;
      end;
      // A unit compiled during Parse (a stale import) is not counted among the build's units
      if ATotal = 0 then
        self.DoShow(NoArgs().Str(LWord).Str(AUnit).Str(self.DoStepWord(AStep))
          .Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_IMPORT));
        return;
      end;
      self.DoShow(NoArgs().Str(LWord).Int(ADone).Int(ATotal).Str(AUnit)
        .Str(self.DoStepWord(AStep)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_LIVE_UNIT));
    end;

    override method PhaseEnded(const APhase: BuildPhase; const AFirst: int64;
      const ASecond: int64; const AThird: int64; const AText: string);
    var
      LNow: int64;
    begin
      lock (self.FLine) do
        LNow := TickCountMs();
        self.DoErase();
        self.FText := "";
        self.FOut.Line(self.DoText(APhase, AFirst, ASecond, AThird, AText,
          DoSeconds(LNow - self.FLast)));
        // Seen as the phase ends even when stdout is a file or a pipe (a build's log)
        FlushOutput();
        self.FLast := LNow;
      end;
    end;

    // The ticker's one wait (its task, DoTick): sleeps until the running phase's next whole
    // second, or until Hold is free (the compile is over); redraws the live line on waking
    // while the compile runs. False once the ticker is to stop
    method Tick(): bool;
    var
      LWait: int64;
      LGo: bool;
    begin
      if atomicload(GLiveQuit) <> 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      lock (self.FLine) do
        LWait := 1000 - ((TickCountMs() - self.FLast) mod 1000);
      end;
      LGo := true;
      trylock (self.Hold) wait LWait do
        LGo := false;
      else
        lock (self.FLine) do
          self.DoDraw();
        end;
      end;
      return LGo and (atomicload(GLiveQuit) = 0);
    end;

    // The compile is over: a live line still on the screen (a phase an error ended) erased,
    // nothing drawn after this
    method Finish();
    begin
      lock (self.FLine) do
        self.DoErase();
        self.FText := "";
        self.FDone := true;
      end;
    end;
  end;

// The ticker task of a live CLIPhases: one Tick after another until it says stop
func DoTick(const APhases: ref CLIPhases);
begin
  while APhases.Tick() do
  end;
end;

// The compile ARequest asks for: AMain checked (ACheck) or built into ARequest.Output
func DoCompile(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ACheck: bool; const APath: string;
  const AOutput: string);
begin
  if ACheck then
    ACompiler.Check(APath);
  else
    ACompiler.Build(APath, AOutput);
  end;
end;

// The compile as DoCompile runs it, with the live phase line when APhases draws one (not nil
// and Live): the compile holds APhases.Hold while it runs, a ticker task redraws the line
// each second meanwhile and stops once Hold is free; the live line is erased at the end on
// every way out (Finish), before any report prints
func DoCompileLive(const APhases: ref CLIPhases; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ACheck: bool; const APath: string; const AOutput: string);
var
  LTicker: task;
begin
  if (APhases = nil) or not APhases.Live() then
    DoCompile(ACompiler, ACheck, APath, AOutput);
    return;
  end;
  lock (APhases.Hold) do
    LTicker := async DoTick(APhases);
    guard
      DoCompile(ACompiler, ACheck, APath, AOutput);
    finally
      APhases.Finish();
    end;
  end;
  await LTicker;
end;

// What -r and -d check before the exe the build wrote runs (AFirst the first report made
// here): a dll (CL0022: only a program loads it; not when AHosted: -d with --host, whose
// host runs it), a lib (CL0023: a program links it in), a target this machine does not run
// (ARuns false: CL0012) is a warning, printed, the build's exit code into ACode and false:
// nothing runs. True when it may run
func DoCanRun(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ARuns: bool; const AHosted: bool;
  const AFirst: int64; var ACode: int32): bool;
begin
  ACode := ACompiler.ExitCode();
  if ACompiler.BuiltDLL and not AHosted then
    ACompiler.Reports.Add(Severity.Warning, ADAM_ERR_CLI_022, NoPlace(), ADAM_MSG_CLI_RUN_DLL,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(AFirst);
    return false;
  end;
  if ACompiler.BuiltLib then
    ACompiler.Reports.Add(Severity.Warning, ADAM_ERR_CLI_023, NoPlace(), ADAM_MSG_CLI_RUN_LIB,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(AFirst);
    return false;
  end;
  if not ARuns then
    ACompiler.Reports.Add(Severity.Warning, ADAM_ERR_CLI_012, NoPlace(), ADAM_MSG_CLI_RUN_FOREIGN,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath).Str(ACompiler.PickedTarget.Triple()));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(AFirst);
    return false;
  end;
  return true;
end;

// adam dap's builder: a source the client launches built for debugging (a debug build,
// whatever its @optimize says) into AOutputPath ("": @outputpath, else output beside it); its
// reports and the build's line as AText; a dll is AIsDLL (debugged in its host); ATarget the
// triple where its @target names none, ATriple the one built for (another one the adapter
// judges). False with why when nothing to launch was written: errors, a lib, no debug file
type
  CLIDAPBuilder = object(DAPBuilder)
    override method Build(const ASource: string; const AOutputPath: string; const ADebug: bool;
      const ALevel: OptLevel; const ALevelGiven: bool; const ATarget: string; var ATriple: string;
      var AExePath: string; var AIsDLL: bool; var ASourceRoot: string; var AText: string): bool;
    var
      LCompiler: ref Compiler;
      LI: int64;
      LTriple: string;
      LStart: int64;
    begin
      AExePath := "";
      AIsDLL := false;
      AText := "";
      ATriple := "";
      LStart := TickCountMs();
      LCompiler := ref Compiler();
      if ATarget <> "" then
        LCompiler.SetDefaultTarget(ATarget);
      end;
      if ADebug then
        LCompiler.SetLevel(OptLevel.Debug);
      else
        if ALevelGiven then
          LCompiler.SetDefaultLevel(ALevel);
        end;
      end;
      LCompiler.Build(SourceFilePath(ASource), AOutputPath);
      for LI := 0 to LCompiler.Reports.Count - 1 do
        AText := AText + LCompiler.Reports.Items[LI].Display() + "\n";
      end;
      if LCompiler.Reports.HasErrors() or (LCompiler.ExePath = "") then
        return false;
      end;
      if LCompiler.BuiltLib then
        AText := AText + NoArgs().Str(LCompiler.ExePath).Fill(ADAM_MSG_DAP_NOT_PROGRAM) + "\n";
        return false;
      end;
      AIsDLL := LCompiler.BuiltDLL;
      LTriple := LCompiler.PickedTarget.Triple();
      ATriple := LTriple;
      // Another target's program: the adapter decides (never debugged, an ELF run)
      if ADebug and (LTriple = DefaultTriple()) and (LCompiler.DebugFilePath = "") then
        AText := AText + NoArgs().Str(LCompiler.ExePath).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_DEBUG_NO_INFO) + "\n";
        return false;
      end;
      AText := AText + NoArgs().Str(ASource).Str(LCompiler.ExePath)
        .Str(DoSeconds(TickCountMs() - LStart)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_BUILT) + "\n";
      AExePath := LCompiler.ExePath;
      // DebugMaker's stable names are from the project root, else bare (the main module's
      // folder)
      ASourceRoot := LCompiler.ProjectRoot;
      if ASourceRoot = "" then
        ASourceRoot := ExtractFileDir(SourceFilePath(ASource));
      end;
      return true;
    end;
  end;

// -d: the exe the build wrote run under Adam's console debugger (Adam.Debug.REPL) in this
// console with ARequest.RunArgs, AMain the main module's file (b <line>'s before a stop).
// DoCanRun's checks first (another target's program is CL0012 as one it does not run; -d on a
// host with no debugger part never gets here: the reader's CL0033); a build that wrote no debug file (not a debug build) is CL0025 and
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS. The exit code of the program's last run; ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS
// when it could not be started
func DoDebugExe(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ARequest: CLIRequest;
  const AMain: string): int32;
var
  LFirst: int64;
  LCode: int32;
  LTriple: string;
  LREPL: ref DebugREPL;
begin
  LFirst := ACompiler.Reports.Count;
  LTriple := ACompiler.PickedTarget.Triple();
  // DLL mode: a dll is debugged in --host, a program never in one
  if ACompiler.BuiltDLL and (len(ARequest.HostPath) = 0) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_029, ADAM_MSG_CLI_DEBUG_DLL_NO_HOST,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  if (not ACompiler.BuiltDLL) and (not ACompiler.BuiltLib) and (len(ARequest.HostPath) > 0) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_030, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HOST_ON_EXE,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  if not DoCanRun(ACompiler, (LTriple = DefaultTriple()) and (DebugTargetFor(LTriple) <> nil),
    ACompiler.BuiltDLL, LFirst, LCode) then
    return LCode;
  end;
  if ACompiler.DebugFilePath = "" then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_025, ADAM_MSG_CLI_DEBUG_NO_INFO,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  FlushOutput();
  LREPL := ref DebugREPL(LTriple, ACompiler.ExePath, ARequest.RunArgs, AMain);
  if ACompiler.BuiltDLL then
    LREPL.SetHost(ARequest.HostPath);
  end;
  if not LREPL.Run() then
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  return LREPL.LastExitCode();
end;

// -r: the exe the build wrote (ACompiler.ExePath), run in the folder it landed in with
// ARequest.RunArgs on adam's own stdin / stdout / stderr; adam's lines are flushed first, so a
// pipe has them ahead of the program's. The program's exit code. Reports made here print on
// their own (the build's printed already): an exe that cannot start is CL0011 and
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS; another target's ELF program runs through RunELF when this host
// runs one (CanRunELF: on win64 WSL); any other target this machine does not run (not the
// registry's default, the host's own) is CL0012, a warning, and the build's exit code,
// nothing run; a dll (M8a,
// which only a program loads) is CL0022, a warning, the same way, and a lib (M8d, which a
// program links in) CL0023
func DoRunExe(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LFirst: int64;
  LExitCode: uint32;
  LCode: int32;
  LHosted: bool;
  LELF: bool;
  LStarted: bool;
begin
  LFirst := ACompiler.Reports.Count;
  LHosted := ACompiler.PickedTarget.Triple() = DefaultTriple();
  // Another target's ELF program runs where this host runs ELF programs (RunELF)
  LELF := false;
  if not LHosted then
    if ACompiler.PickedTarget.ProgramFormat() = ImageFormat.ELF then
      LELF := CanRunELF();
    end;
  end;
  if not DoCanRun(ACompiler, LHosted or LELF, false, LFirst, LCode) then
    return LCode;
  end;
  FlushOutput();
  if LELF then
    LStarted := RunELF(ACompiler.ExePath, ARequest.RunArgs, ExtractFileDir(ACompiler.ExePath),
      LExitCode);
  else
    LStarted := RunAttached(ACompiler.ExePath, ARequest.RunArgs,
      ExtractFileDir(ACompiler.ExePath), LExitCode);
  end;
  if not LStarted then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_011, ADAM_MSG_CLI_RUN_FAILED,
      NoArgs().Str(ACompiler.ExePath));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  return int32(LExitCode);
end;

// The project folder ARequest.Positional names (none given: the current folder), resolved,
// in ADir: it must hold a project.toml, never one searched for above it (PaskalCPP's build /
// pack [<folder>]). ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE with the reports printed:
// the folder cannot be resolved (CL0014) or holds no project.toml (CL0013)
func DoProjectFolder(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ACommands: CommandTable;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest; var ADir: string): int32;
begin
  if ARequest.Positional = "" then
    ADir := ResolvePath(".");
  else
    ADir := ResolvePath(ARequest.Positional);
  end;
  if ADir = "" then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_014, ADAM_MSG_CLI_BAD_PROJECT_DIR,
      NoArgs().Str(ARequest.Positional).Str(DoSee(ACommands, ARequest.Command)));
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE;
  end;
  if not FileExists(ResolvePath(ADAM_PROJECT_FILE_NAME, ADir)) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_013, ADAM_MSG_CLI_NO_PROJECT,
      NoArgs().Str(ADAM_PROJECT_FILE_NAME).Str(ADir).Str(DoSee(ACommands, ARequest.Command)));
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// build's main module in AMain: ARequest.Positional when it is no folder (a file, its .adam
// implied by SourceFilePath, as check's); else the main module of the project whose project.toml is in that folder
// (DoProjectFolder). ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else the exit code with the reports printed:
// DoProjectFolder's mistakes, or a project.toml that does not load (its PJ reports,
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS)
func DoBuildMain(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ACommands: CommandTable;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest; var AMain: string): int32;
var
  LDir: string;
  LCode: int32;
  LProject: ref Project;
begin
  AMain := ARequest.Positional;
  if (AMain <> "") and not DirectoryExists(AMain) then
    AMain := SourceFilePath(AMain);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  LCode := DoProjectFolder(ACompiler, ACommands, ARequest, LDir);
  if LCode <> ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK then
    return LCode;
  end;
  // Read once with no reports for its main module: the build reads it again and reports
  // what it says, so each report is printed once. One that does not load is read again into
  // the reports to say why
  LProject := ref Project(nil);
  if not LProject.Load(LDir) then
    LProject := ref Project(ACompiler.Reports);
    if not LProject.Load(LDir) then
      ACompiler.PrintReports();
      return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
    end;
  end;
  AMain := LProject.MainPath();
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// The word a report's severity has in adam info's JSON (a fixed word, never a message text)
func DoSeverityWord(const ALevel: Severity): string;
begin
  match ALevel of
    Severity.Hint: return "hint";
    Severity.Warning: return "warning";
    Severity.Error: return "error";
    Severity.Fatal: return "fatal";
  end;
  return "error";
end;

// adam info [<folder>] (see the header): the project as one line of JSON, every report of its
// load in it (a folder that cannot be resolved is CL0014 there); ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK
func DoInfo(const ACommands: CommandTable; const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LReports: ref Diagnostics;
  LProject: ref Project;
  LDir: string;
  LHasFile: bool;
  LValid: bool;
  LJSON: JSON;
  LItem: JSON;
  LFresh: JSON;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LReports := ref Diagnostics(ADAM_CLI_INFO_REPORT_BUDGET);
  if ARequest.Positional = "" then
    LDir := ResolvePath(".");
  else
    LDir := ResolvePath(ARequest.Positional);
  end;
  LHasFile := false;
  LValid := false;
  if LDir = "" then
    DoReport(LReports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_014, ADAM_MSG_CLI_BAD_PROJECT_DIR,
      NoArgs().Str(ARequest.Positional).Str(DoSee(ACommands, ARequest.Command)));
  else
    LHasFile := FileExists(ResolvePath(ADAM_PROJECT_FILE_NAME, LDir));
  end;
  LProject := ref Project(LReports);
  if LHasFile then
    LValid := LProject.Load(LDir);
  end;
  LJSON.Add("format", ADAM_CLI_INFO_FORMAT);
  LJSON.Add("project", LHasFile);
  LJSON.Add("valid", LValid);
  LJSON.Add("root", ForwardSlashes(LDir));
  if LValid then
    LJSON.Add("file", ForwardSlashes(LProject.FileName));
    LJSON.Add("name", LProject.ProjectName);
    LJSON.Add("kind", ProjectKindText(LProject.Kind));
    LJSON.Add("main", ForwardSlashes(LProject.MainPath()));
    LJSON.Add("output", ForwardSlashes(LProject.OutputPath()));
    LJSON.Add("rez", ForwardSlashes(LProject.RezPath()));
  end;
  LJSON.BeginArray("reports");
  for LI := 0 to LReports.Count - 1 do
    LItem := LFresh;
    LItem.Add("severity", DoSeverityWord(LReports.Items[LI].Level));
    LItem.Add("code", LReports.Items[LI].Code);
    LItem.Add("message", LReports.Items[LI].Text());
    LJSON.Add(LItem);
  end;
  LJSON.EndArray();
  println("{}", LJSON.ToString());
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// adam init <name> <type>: the new project in the working folder (Adam.Driver.Project's
// Scaffold, its reports into the compile's Diagnostics), then, not under --quiet, where it
// was made and how to build it. ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS with the
// reports printed
func DoInit(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LKind: ModuleKind;
  LProject: ref Project;
begin
  // DoRead has checked the type: a type it turned away never gets here
  if not ProjectKindFromText(ARequest.TypeText, LKind) then
    return ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE;
  end;
  LProject := ref Project(ACompiler.Reports);
  if not LProject.Scaffold("", ARequest.Positional, LKind) then
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ProjectKindText(LKind)).Str(ARequest.Positional)
      .Str(LProject.Root).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_INIT_DONE));
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ARequest.Positional).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_INIT_NEXT));
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// The loaded project's assets folder, checked (CL0017 when it is not there), in AAssets and
// its archive's path, its folder made (CL0018 when it cannot be), in ARez: <name>.rez in the
// output folder itself (Project.RezPath), one archive for every target and mode, which each
// build copies beside its exe. False, reported
func DoPackPaths(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const AProject: ref Project;
  var AAssets: string; var ARez: string): bool;
var
  LFolder: string;
begin
  AAssets := AProject.AssetsPath();
  ARez := AProject.RezPath();
  if (AAssets = "") or not DirectoryExists(AAssets) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_017, ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_NO_ASSETS,
      NoArgs().Str(ResolvePath(ADAM_PROJECT_ASSETS_DIR, AProject.Root)));
    return false;
  end;
  LFolder := ExtractFileDir(ARez);
  if (ARez = "") or not ForceDirectories(LFolder) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_018, ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_FOLDER,
      NoArgs().Str(AProject.OutputPath()));
    return false;
  end;
  return true;
end;

// The archive ARez adam pack just wrote, copied over every older copy a build left beside
// its exe (CopyRez): each <output>\bin\<triple>\<mode>\ folder already holding <name>.rez, so
// a program built before the pack opens the new assets with no rebuild; each one printed
// unless AQuiet. No bin folder yet: nothing to update. False, reported (CL0021), when a copy
// cannot be written
func DoPackRefresh(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ARez: string; const AQuiet: bool): bool;
var
  LBin: string;
  LTriples: StringArray;
  LModes: StringArray;
  LTripleDir: string;
  LDir: string;
  LCopy: string;
  LI: int64;
  LJ: int64;
begin
  LBin := ResolvePath(ADAM_OUTPUT_BIN_DIR, ExtractFileDir(ARez));
  if (LBin = "") or not GetDirectories(LBin, LTriples) then
    return true;
  end;
  for LI := 0 to len(LTriples) - 1 do
    LTripleDir := ResolvePath(LTriples[LI], LBin);
    if GetDirectories(LTripleDir, LModes) then
      for LJ := 0 to len(LModes) - 1 do
        LDir := ResolvePath(LModes[LJ], LTripleDir);
        if FileExists(ResolvePath(ExtractFileName(ARez), LDir)) then
          if not CopyRez(ARez, LDir, LCopy) then
            DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_021, ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_COPY,
              NoArgs().Str(ARez).Str(LCopy));
            return false;
          end;
          if not AQuiet then
            AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(LCopy).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_UPDATED));
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  return true;
end;

// adam pack [<folder>]: the assets folder of the project whose project.toml is in that folder
// (DoProjectFolder) zipped into its <name>.rez in the output folder (DoPackPaths) with its
// pack password, by System.CustomIO's ZipDirectoryContents (deflated, ZipCrypto unless the
// password is empty, entries named below assets/). Not under --quiet: the start, each entry,
// the count and the archive written (PaskalCPP's AssetPacker lines), then each older copy
// beside a built exe updated (DoPackRefresh). ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else DoProjectFolder's
// mistakes (exit 2) or ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS with the reports printed: a project.toml that
// does not load (its PJ reports), no assets folder, the archive's folder, the archive itself
// (CL0019, ZipLastError's reason) or a copy beside an exe (CL0021)
// adam editor [<file> ...] (pcpp's): the packaged editor (ADAM_CLI_EDITOR_EXE) started on its
// own in its own folder, never waited for, each file made a full path (the editor's working
// folder is its own); the editor opens them (a missing one is its to report). The editor
// missing (CL0031) or a start that failed (CL0032): reported, ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS
func DoEditor(const ACompiler: ref Compiler; const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LEditor: string;
  LArgs: StringArray;
  LExitCode: uint32;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LEditor := ResolvePath(ADAM_CLI_EDITOR_EXE);
  if (LEditor = "") or not FileExists(LEditor) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_031, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EDITOR_MISSING,
      NoArgs().Str(ADAM_CLI_EDITOR_EXE));
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  setlength(LArgs, len(ARequest.Files));
  for LI := 0 to len(ARequest.Files) - 1 do
    LArgs[LI] := ResolvePath(ARequest.Files[LI]);
  end;
  if not RunPE(LEditor, LArgs, ExtractFileDir(LEditor), false, LExitCode) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_032, ADAM_MSG_CLI_EDITOR_FAILED,
      NoArgs().Str(LEditor));
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

func DoPack(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ACommands: CommandTable; const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LDir: string;
  LCode: int32;
  LProject: ref Project;
  LAssets: string;
  LRez: string;
  LEntries: int64;
  LFirst: int64;
begin
  LCode := DoProjectFolder(ACompiler, ACommands, ARequest, LDir);
  if LCode <> ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK then
    return LCode;
  end;
  LProject := ref Project(ACompiler.Reports);
  if not LProject.Load(LDir) or not DoPackPaths(ACompiler, LProject, LAssets, LRez) then
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  // project.toml's warnings (an unknown key) before the pack's own lines; a failure below
  // prints only what it adds
  ACompiler.PrintReports();
  LFirst := ACompiler.Reports.Count;
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(LAssets).Str(LRez).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_START));
  end;
  // The progress routine (a closure over LEntries): each entry counted once, on its first
  // call, and printed indented unless quiet
  LEntries := 0;
  if not ZipDirectoryContents(LRez, LAssets, LProject.Password, "",
    func(const AEntry: string; const APercent: int32; const ANewFile: bool)
    begin
      if ANewFile then
        LEntries := LEntries + 1;
        if not ARequest.Quiet then
          println("{}", NoArgs().Str(AEntry).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_ENTRY));
        end;
      end;
    end) then
    DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_019, ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_FAILED,
      NoArgs().Str(LAssets).Str(LRez).Str(ZipLastError()));
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Int(LEntries).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_COUNT));
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(LRez).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_PACK_DONE));
  end;
  if not DoPackRefresh(AOut, ACompiler, LRez, ARequest.Quiet) then
    ACompiler.Reports.PrintFrom(LFirst);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// AText (its lines ended by LF, or by CRLF where a spec's [[insert]] text came from a CRLF
// file) as the file adam cimport writes: every line CRLF-ended, as adam init writes its
// sources, the same bytes on every host
func DoCImportFileText(const AText: string): string;
begin
  return ReplaceStr(ReplaceStr(AText, "\r\n", "\n"), "\n", "\r\n");
end;

// The unit ASpec writes imported for ATriple (adam cimport, see DoCImport) into AText (lines
// LF-ended, no [[insert]] applied) with the writer that wrote it in AWriter: the search's roots
// set (the spec's include folders for ATriple, then the target's system headers), each header
// the spec names found (as an #include <...> is), then preprocessed in order (predefines, the
// spec's defines and undefines for ATriple, the headers), parsed and written, its first line
// naming ATriples. Not under --quiet: the import's line (the unit, the target, the unit's
// file) and each header's, as found. --emit-pp: the preprocessed text printed, AEmitted true
// and nothing written. False after a report
func DoCImportTarget(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest; const ASpec: ref ImportSpec; const ATriple: string;
  const ATriples: StringArray; var AText: string; var AWriter: ref CUnitWriter;
  var AEmitted: bool): bool;
var
  LSearch: ref HeaderSearch;
  LPre: ref Preprocessor;
  LTarget: ref Target;
  LFolders: StringArray;
  LDefines: SpecDefineArray;
  LUndefines: StringArray;
  LLines: StringArray;
  LFound: HeaderFile;
  LFiles: array of HeaderFile;
  LParser: ref CParser;
  LSources: StringArray;
  LOk: bool;
  LI: int64;
begin
  AText := "";
  AWriter := nil;
  AEmitted := false;
  LSearch := ref HeaderSearch(ACompiler.Reports);
  LOk := true;
  LFolders := ASpec.IncludesFor(ATriple);
  for LI := 0 to len(LFolders) - 1 do
    if not LSearch.AddIncludeFolder(LFolders[LI], ATriple, false, ASpec.PlaceOf(0, 0)) then
      LOk := false;
    end;
  end;
  LFolders := ASpec.SystemIncludesFor(ATriple);
  for LI := 0 to len(LFolders) - 1 do
    if not LSearch.AddIncludeFolder(LFolders[LI], ATriple, true, ASpec.PlaceOf(0, 0)) then
      LOk := false;
    end;
  end;
  if not LSearch.AddSystemRoots(ATriple) then
    LOk := false;
  end;
  if not LOk then
    return false;
  end;
  setlength(LFiles, len(ASpec.Headers));
  for LI := 0 to len(ASpec.Headers) - 1 do
    if LSearch.Find(ASpec.Headers[LI].Text, false, NoHeader(), false, LFound) then
      LFiles[LI] := LFound;
    else
      LSearch.ReportMissing(ASpec.Headers[LI].Text, ASpec.TextPlace(ASpec.Headers[LI]));
      LOk := false;
    end;
  end;
  if not LOk then
    return false;
  end;
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ASpec.UnitName).Str(ATriple)
      .Str(ForwardSlashes(ASpec.UnitPath(ARequest.Output))).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_CIMPORT_START));
    for LI := 0 to len(LFiles) - 1 do
      AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ASpec.Headers[LI].Text).Str(LFiles[LI].FullName)
        .Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_CIMPORT_HEADER));
    end;
  end;
  LTarget := FindTarget(ATriple);
  LPre := ref Preprocessor(ACompiler.Reports, LSearch, ATriple, LTarget.CharSigned());
  if LPre.Predefine() then
    LDefines := ASpec.DefinesFor(ATriple);
    for LI := 0 to len(LDefines) - 1 do
      LPre.Define(LDefines[LI].Name, LDefines[LI].Value);
    end;
    LUndefines := ASpec.UndefinesFor(ATriple);
    for LI := 0 to len(LUndefines) - 1 do
      LPre.Undefine(LUndefines[LI]);
    end;
    for LI := 0 to len(LFiles) - 1 do
      LPre.Include(LFiles[LI], ASpec.TextPlace(ASpec.Headers[LI]));
    end;
  end;
  if ACompiler.Reports.HasErrors() then
    return false;
  end;
  if ARequest.EmitPp then
    // clang -E's window: the preprocessed text, nothing parsed or written
    LLines := LPre.EmitLines();
    for LI := 0 to len(LLines) - 1 do
      AOut.Line(LLines[LI]);
    end;
    AEmitted := true;
    return true;
  end;
  LParser := ref CParser(ACompiler.Reports, LPre, LTarget);
  if not LParser.Parse() then
    return false;
  end;
  // the declarations bound: the spec's sources, else each spec header's own folder
  LSources := ASpec.Sources;
  if len(LSources) = 0 then
    setlength(LSources, len(LFiles));
    for LI := 0 to len(LFiles) - 1 do
      LSources[LI] := ExtractFileDir(LFiles[LI].FullName);
    end;
  end;
  AWriter := ref CUnitWriter(ACompiler.Reports, ASpec, LPre, LParser, ATriple, LSources);
  AWriter.SetHeaderTargets(ATriples);
  if not AWriter.Write(AText) then
    return false;
  end;
  AText := ReplaceStr(AText, "\r\n", "\n");
  return true;
end;

// The layout probe of the unit APath for ATriple (M9g): the unit checked by AChecker's front
// end on that target (each target its own compiler: one front end per compiler), the probe
// from AWriter's records written beside the unit when the spec asks (one file per target
// when AOneTarget is false) and printed under --emit-layout. False after a report
func DoCImportLayout(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const AChecker: ref Compiler;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest; const ASpec: ref ImportSpec; const ATriple: string;
  const AOneTarget: bool; const APath: string; const AWriter: ref CUnitWriter): bool;
var
  LProbe: string;
  LProbePath: string;
  LLines: StringArray;
  LI: int64;
begin
  AChecker.SetTarget(ATriple);
  AChecker.CheckUnit(APath);
  if AChecker.Reports.HasErrors() then
    return false;
  end;
  LProbe := WriteLayoutProbe(AChecker.Tree, AChecker.PickedTarget, AChecker.MainModule,
    ASpec, ATriple, AWriter.Probes());
  if ASpec.LayoutProbe then
    LProbePath := ASpec.LayoutProbePath(ARequest.Output, ATriple, AOneTarget);
    if not WriteAllText(LProbePath, DoCImportFileText(LProbe)) then
      AChecker.Reports.Add(Severity.Error, ADAM_ERR_CIMPORT_WRITER_004, NoPlace(),
        ADAM_MSG_CIMPORT_WRITER_WRITE_FAILED, NoArgs().Str(ForwardSlashes(LProbePath)));
      return false;
    end;
    if not ARequest.Quiet then
      AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(ForwardSlashes(LProbePath)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_CIMPORT_PROBE));
    end;
  end;
  if ARequest.EmitLayout then
    LLines := SplitString(LProbe, "\n");
    for LI := 0 to len(LLines) - 2 do
      AOut.Line(LLines[LI]);
    end;
  end;
  return true;
end;

// adam cimport <spec>: the import spec read and checked (Adam.CImport.Spec), then imported for
// each of its targets (ImportTargets: -t's alone, else the spec's targets, else the
// registry's default; DoCImportTarget) and the targets' texts merged into one unit
// (Adam.CImport.Merge: what differs under @ifdef TARGET_<triple>), the spec's [[insert]]s
// applied to it once and the unit written (--emit-unit: its text; not under --quiet: the
// counts, the first target's). --emit-pp: each target's preprocessed text, and nothing more.
// layoutprobe / --emit-layout: a layout probe per target (DoCImportLayout).
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS with the CP / CC / CI reports
func DoCImport(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LSpec: ref ImportSpec;
  LTriples: StringArray;
  LTexts: StringArray;
  LWriters: array of ref CUnitWriter;
  LEmitted: bool;
  LChecker: ref Compiler;
  LLines: StringArray;
  LCounts: WriterCounts;
  LText: string;
  LPath: string;
  LOk: bool;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LSpec := ref ImportSpec(ACompiler.Reports);
  if not LSpec.Load(ARequest.Positional) then
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  LTriples := LSpec.ImportTargets(ARequest.TargetTriple, DefaultTriple());
  setlength(LTexts, len(LTriples));
  setlength(LWriters, len(LTriples));
  for LI := 0 to len(LTriples) - 1 do
    if not DoCImportTarget(AOut, ACompiler, ARequest, LSpec, LTriples[LI], LTriples, LTexts[LI],
      LWriters[LI], LEmitted) then
      ACompiler.PrintReports();
      return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
    end;
  end;
  if ARequest.EmitPp then
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  // one unit for every target, then the spec's edits on its final text
  LText := MergeTargetTexts(LTriples, LTexts);
  if not LWriters[0].ApplyInserts(LText) then
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  // the unit's lines LF-ended in memory (--emit-unit prints them), CRLF in its file
  LText := ReplaceStr(LText, "\r\n", "\n");
  LPath := LSpec.UnitPath(ARequest.Output);
  if not ForceDirectories(ExtractFileDir(LPath)) or
    not WriteAllText(LPath, DoCImportFileText(LText)) then
    ACompiler.Reports.Add(Severity.Error, ADAM_ERR_CIMPORT_WRITER_004, NoPlace(),
      ADAM_MSG_CIMPORT_WRITER_WRITE_FAILED, NoArgs().Str(ForwardSlashes(LPath)));
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
  end;
  if ARequest.EmitUnit then
    LLines := SplitString(LText, "\n");
    // the text ends in a newline: no empty line after it
    for LI := 0 to len(LLines) - 2 do
      AOut.Line(LLines[LI]);
    end;
  end;
  if LSpec.LayoutProbe or ARequest.EmitLayout then
    // the layout proof (M9g): the unit as Adam's front end lays it out on each target, the
    // first on this compiler, each other on a compiler of its own
    for LI := 0 to len(LTriples) - 1 do
      LChecker := ACompiler;
      if LI > 0 then
        LChecker := ref Compiler();
      end;
      LOk := DoCImportLayout(AOut, LChecker, ARequest, LSpec, LTriples[LI], len(LTriples) = 1,
        LPath, LWriters[LI]);
      if LI > 0 then
        LChecker.PrintReports();
      end;
      if not LOk then
        ACompiler.PrintReports();
        return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
      end;
    end;
  end;
  ACompiler.PrintReports();
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    LCounts := LWriters[0].Counts();
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Int(LCounts.Routines).Int(LCounts.Variables).Int(LCounts.Types)
      .Int(LCounts.Constants).Int(LCounts.Unbound).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_CIMPORT_DONE));
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
end;

// Runs the command line ARequest read: a help printed into AOut, or the compile it asks for
// run and its reports printed. The exit code
func DoRun(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ACommands: CommandTable; const AOptions: OptionTable; const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LSpec: CommandSpec;
  LTopic: int64;
  LStart: int64;
  LPhases: ref CLIPhases;
  LCode: int32;
  LMain: string;
  LNoPaths: StringArray;
begin
  if ARequest.Command < 0 then
    DoHelpAll(AOut, ACommands, AOptions);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  if ARequest.WantHelp then
    DoHelpCommand(AOut, ACommands, AOptions, ARequest.Command);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  LSpec := ACommands[ARequest.Command];
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Help then
    if ARequest.Positional = "" then
      DoHelpAll(AOut, ACommands, AOptions);
      return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
    end;
    LTopic := DoFindCommand(ACommands, ARequest.Positional);
    if LTopic < 0 then
      DoReport(ACompiler.Reports, ADAM_ERR_CLI_006, ADAM_MSG_CLI_HELP_UNKNOWN,
        NoArgs().Str(ARequest.Positional));
      ACompiler.PrintReports();
      return ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE;
    end;
    DoHelpCommand(AOut, ACommands, AOptions, LTopic);
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Init then
    return DoInit(AOut, ACompiler, ARequest);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.DAP then
    return RunDAP(ref ProtocolTransport(ref StdioChannel()), ref CLIDAPBuilder());
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.LSP then
    setlength(LNoPaths, 0);
    return RunLSP(ref ProtocolTransport(ref StdioChannel()), LNoPaths);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Editor then
    return DoEditor(ACompiler, ARequest);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Pack then
    return DoPack(AOut, ACompiler, ACommands, ARequest);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Info then
    return DoInfo(ACommands, ARequest);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.CImport then
    return DoCImport(AOut, ACompiler, ARequest);
  end;
  if ARequest.TargetTriple <> "" then
    if ARequest.Defaults then
      ACompiler.SetDefaultTarget(ARequest.TargetTriple);
    else
      ACompiler.SetTarget(ARequest.TargetTriple);
    end;
  end;
  // A line per phase as it ends (not under --quiet); made here so the first phase's time
  // starts with the compile
  LPhases := nil;
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    LPhases := ref CLIPhases(AOut);
    ACompiler.SetListener(LPhases);
  end;
  if LSpec.Id = CLICommand.Check then
    DoCompileLive(LPhases, ACompiler, true, SourceFilePath(ARequest.Positional), "");
    ACompiler.PrintReports();
    return ACompiler.ExitCode();
  end;
  LStart := TickCountMs();
  LCode := DoBuildMain(ACompiler, ACommands, ARequest, LMain);
  if LCode <> ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK then
    return LCode;
  end;
  DoCompileLive(LPhases, ACompiler, false, LMain, ARequest.Output);
  ACompiler.PrintReports();
  // The status line: a build that wrote its exe says so, the main module (as given, or the
  // project's) and the exe as written, with the time it took (not under --quiet)
  if not ARequest.Quiet and (ACompiler.ExePath <> "") then
    AOut.Line(NoArgs().Str(LMain).Str(ACompiler.ExePath)
      .Str(DoSeconds(TickCountMs() - LStart)).Fill(ADAM_MSG_CLI_BUILT));
  end;
  // -r: the program runs once its exe is written (a failed build never runs it)
  if ARequest.Run and (ACompiler.ExePath <> "") then
    return DoRunExe(ACompiler, ARequest);
  end;
  // -d: the program runs under the console debugger once its exe is written
  if ARequest.Debug and (ACompiler.ExePath <> "") then
    return DoDebugExe(ACompiler, ARequest, LMain);
  end;
  return ACompiler.ExitCode();
end;

// adam --dev-editor: Adam.Dev.Editor's job, its status lines (not under --quiet) and reports
// printed; ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK, else ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS
func DoDevEditor(const AOut: ref HelpOut; const ACompiler: ref Compiler;
  const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
var
  LLines: StringArray;
  LOk: bool;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LOk := DevEditor(ACompiler.Reports, LLines);
  if not ARequest.Quiet then
    for LI := 0 to len(LLines) - 1 do
      AOut.Line(LLines[LI]);
    end;
  end;
  ACompiler.PrintReports();
  if LOk then
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
end;

// adam --dev-build-adam: Adam.Dev.BuildAdam's job (its lines are its own, as it goes);
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK after BUILD OK, else ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS
func DoDevBuildAdam(): int32;
begin
  if DevBuildAdam() then
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
end;

// adam --dev-pack <spec>: Adam.Dev.Pack's job (its lines are its own, as it goes);
// ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK after PACK OK, else ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS
func DoDevPack(const ARequest: CLIRequest): int32;
begin
  if DevPack(ARequest.DevPackSpec) then
    return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_OK;
  end;
  return ADAM_DRIVER_EXIT_ERRORS;
end;

// Runs adam's command line (see the header): the exit code for the process
public func RunCommandLine(): int32;
var
  LCompiler: ref Compiler;
  LCommands: CommandTable;
  LOptions: OptionTable;
  LAllCommands: CommandTable;
  LAllOptions: OptionTable;
  LRequest: CLIRequest;
  LColor: bool;
  LOut: ref HelpOut;
begin
  // adam's own heap report only with --heap (System.Runtime's one public routine)
  SetHeapReport(false);
  // Color only on a console that takes VT sequences; piped or redirected, every line is
  // plain (what a file, another program and adamtest read)
  LColor := EscapesEnabled();
  LOut := ref HelpOut(LColor);
  LCompiler := ref Compiler();
  LCompiler.Reports.SetColor(LColor);
  // What this host has drives the help and the reader; what it lacks is only named (CL0033)
  LAllCommands := DoCommandTable();
  LAllOptions := DoOptionTable();
  LCommands := DoHostCommands(LAllCommands, true);
  LOptions := DoHostOptions(LAllOptions, true);
  if not DoWantsNoBanner(LOptions) then
    DoBanner(LOut);
  end;
  if not DoRead(LCommands, LOptions, DoHostCommands(LAllCommands, false),
    DoHostOptions(LAllOptions, false), LCompiler.Reports, LRequest) then
    LCompiler.PrintReports();
    return ADAM_CLI_EXIT_USAGE;
  end;
  if LRequest.Heap then
    SetHeapReport(true);
  end;
  if LRequest.DevEditor then
    return DoDevEditor(LOut, LCompiler, LRequest);
  end;
  if LRequest.DevBuildAdam then
    return DoDevBuildAdam();
  end;
  if LRequest.DevPack then
    return DoDevPack(LRequest);
  end;
  LCompiler.SetEmitIR(LRequest.EmitIR);
  // The build's level, set before the front end runs (every file's DEBUG / RELEASE /
  // RELEASE_<LEVEL> define reads it): -opt's, else the compiler's own build at safe, else the
  // main module's @optimize decides
  if LRequest.LevelGiven then
    if LRequest.Defaults then
      LCompiler.SetDefaultLevel(LRequest.Level);
    else
      LCompiler.SetLevel(LRequest.Level);
    end;
  else
    if LRequest.SelfBuild then
      LCompiler.SetLevel(OptLevel.Safe);
    end;
  end;
  return DoRun(LOut, LCompiler, LCommands, LOptions, LRequest);
end;

end.
